hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4009","(4009) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Our sheikhs did not They tilt, meaning when one of them raises his head from the second prostration in the first and third rak’ahs, he gets up as Yes, and he did not sit."
"4010","(4010) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was quicker to stand in the first rak’ah than in the last prostration."
"4011","(4011) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Abi Ayyash, who said: I realized more than one person. One of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Whenever he raised his head from prostration in the first raka’ah and the third, he would stand as if And he did not sit."
"4012","(4012) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Khaled, he said: I saw Abu Qalababi and Al-Hasan relying on their hands to Prayer"
"4013","(4013) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in a man relying on his hands when he got up to pray."
"4014","(4014) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated it"
"4015","(4015) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahadi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated that, unless he was very old or sick."
"4016","(4016) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Tell me who saw lions, mutilated, and stolen ones relying on On their hands when they get up."
"4017","(4017) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: I saw a Qais leaning on his hands when he got up."
"4018","(4018) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I saw Ibn Umar getting up for prayer. And he relies on his hands."
"4019","(4019) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was relying on his hands."
"4020","(4020) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ziyad bin Zayd al-Sawai’i, on the authority of Abu Juhaif. On the authority of Ali, he said: It is part of the Sunnah in the obligatory prayer that if a man gets up for the first two rak’ahs, he should not rely on it. With his hands on the ground, unless he is old and unable to do so. (Bayhaqi 136)"
"4021","(4021) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Medi ibn Maimun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He hated to be baptized, but Al-Hasan used to be baptized."
"4022","(4022) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Dhudhail bin Bilal, who said: I saw Ata being baptized when he got up."
"4023","(4023) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: Malik bin Al-Huwaithir used to come to us and say: Shall I not tell you about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? So he prays at a time other than that of the prayer, so when he raises his head from the second prostration in the first rak’ah, he stands up sitting, then He rose and was baptized. (Bukhari 823, Abu Dawud 840)"
"4024","(4024) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who did not recite the opening of the Book? He said: If he recited something else, that will be sufficient."
"4025","(4025) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I asked Abraham about a man who forgets to open the book. So he recites a surah, or recites the Opening of the Book, and does he not recite anything along with it? He said: It is sufficient."
"4026","(4026) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and Al-Hakam; Concerning a man who forgot and opened the book, Al-Sha’bi said: He prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and Al-Hakam said: He recites it when he remembers."
"4027","(4027) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who recited, “Say, ‘He is Allah, One,’” and forgot, so he opened the Book and said, “It is sufficient.”"
"4028","(4028) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama, he said: Omar prayed the Maghrib prayer but did not recite. When he left, the people said to him: You did not recite. He said: How was it that the bowing and prostration were complete? He? They said: Yes, and he said: There is no problem, I was talking to myself about a camel that I prepared with its bags and suitcases."
"4029","(4029) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: If a man prays, he forgets to even recite. He finished his prayer and said: What all people recite is sufficient."
"4030","(4030) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan (H) and on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders; About a man who forgot to recite the recitation at noon and afternoon until he finished his prayer. They said: It is sufficient for him if he completed the bowing. And prostration."
"4031","(4031) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: A man came to Ali and said: I prayed. And I forgot to read? He said to him: Have you completed your bowing and prostration? He said: Yes, he said: It suffices you."
"4032","(4032) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If the Qur’an forgets, then he does not observe the iddah. With that rak'ah"
"4033","(4033) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abu Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no prayer except with the people of the Qur’an."
"4034","(4034) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, who said: Umar prayed the Maghrib prayer but did not recite it. And when he left, they said to him: O Commander of the Faithful, you did not recite. He said: I spoke to myself while I was praying. I brought a camel from Medina, and I continued to prepare it until it entered the Levant. He said: Then he repeated the prayer and the recitation."
"4035","(4035) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: When he said the greatest, he would remain silent, seeking not to read. So he said the takbir, then bowed before he recited, then he raised his head and recited, and motioned not to kneel, and he opened the Qur’an with (Praise be to God). Lord of the worlds)"
"4036","(4036) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you kneel and raise your head, recite if you wish after you raise your head. your head, then kneel, and if you wish, prostrate as you are."
"4037","(4037) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Qais, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, who said: The mosque was sprinkled and it was built on The era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr. (Bukhari 458, Abu Dawud 3195)"
"4038","(4038) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Kathir bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab; Omar bin Al-Khattab came to the Quba Mosque on a horse he owned and prayed there, then he said: O Yarfa, bring me a newspaper. He said: So he brought him a newspaper, and Omar kept his garment, then swept it away."
"4039","(4039) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Asim Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, saying: I was with Al-Sha’bi in the mosque, and he started to stutter. So I said: What are you doing, Abu Amr? He said: Did you pick up the reeds, the rattles, and other things from the mosque? He said: Abu Asim was blind."
"4040","(4040) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, who said: I saw Salim sweeping a place, then he prayed in it."
"4041","(4041) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Zaid; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to cover the dust of the mosque with a newspaper."
"4042","(4042) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Tirmidhi 331, Ahmad 1/358)"
"4043","(4043) Abbad bin Al-Awwam and Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, he said: You informed me. Maimoonah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray over wine. (Bukhari 333 and Abu Dawud 656)"
"4044","(4044) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Sa’id; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on a mat. (Muslim 271. Ahmad 3/10)"
"4045","(4045) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, on the authority of Umm Sulaym; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray in her house over wine. (Nasa’i 816. Ahmad 6/377)"
"4046","(4046) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Umm Kulthum; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray over wine. (Ahmad 6/302, Abu Ali 6884)"
"4047","(4047) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Al-Azraq ibn Qays, on the authority of Dhakwan, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He used to pray over the wine. (Ahmad 6/209, Tayalisi 1544)"
"4048","(4048) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Anas Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid Ibn al-Mundhir Ibn al-Jaroud On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: He prepared some of my ummah for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, as food, and he said: I would like you to eat it. My house and you prayed in it. He said: Then one of those stallions came to him and in the house, so he ordered a side of it to be swept and sprinkled. So he prayed and we prayed with him. (Ahmad 3/112, Abu Ali 4227)"
"4049","(4049) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to pray over wine."
"4050","(4050) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Dharr narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir, who said: I saw Jabir bin Abdullah praying. On a mat of papyrus."
"4051","(4051) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Umari told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on a mat. (Bukhari 380, Abu Dawud 612)"
"4052","(4052) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: I saw him praying on the mat and prostrating. Aliyah"
"4053","(4053) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Safwan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr; He used to pray over wine."
"4054","(4054) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Thabit bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I saw Zayd bin Thabit praying on a mat. He prostrates on it."
"4055","(4055) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, who said: Tell me who saw Zayd ibn Thabit praying. Ali Hasir."
"4056","(4056) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Toubah al-Anbari, on the authority of Nafi`, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to pray on a mat."
"4057","(4057) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Praying over a wine drinker is a Sunnah."
"4058","(4058) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, who said: I prayed with Ibn Abbas in his house, with a veil prostrating. Aliyah"
"4059","(4059) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Issa bin Sinan, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz praying on a veil."
"4060","(4060) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jabir; He prayed upon anointing."
"4061","(4061) Aidh bin Habib narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man from Bakr bin Wael, who said: I saw Ali praying for Praying in sackcloth, he kneels on it and prostrates."
"4062","(4062) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubair bin Nufayr; That Abu Darda’ used to pray on a sackcloth and prostrate on it."
"4063","(4063) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad and his companions; They hated to pray on clothes, furs, and sackcloths."
"4064","(4064) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayyan, on the authority of Shaqiq bin Salamah, who said: I prayed with Ibn Masoud Ali. He anointed himself, and he used to prostrate on it."
"4065","(4065) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah al-Dhab`i, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was mingling with us, and he would say to a brother of mine: O Abu Umayr, what did Al-Naghir do? He said: And he sprinkled water. As a carpet for us, may the blessings of God be upon him. (Bukhari 6129. Muslim 1692)"
"4066","(4066) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zam`a, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, and Salamah ibn Wahram, one of them said: On the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on a carpet. (Ahmad 232. Hakim 259)"
"4067","(4067) Abdullah bin Mubarak and Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Sawda, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, said: I would not care if you prayed on six pillars, one on top of the other."
"4068","(4068) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jibran, he said: Ibn Abbas led us in prayer on the verge of death. The Maghrib prayer entered the House."
"4069","(4069) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, he said: I saw a place where he said to Abraham: I saw Abu Wael. He prayed over my soul, and Ibrahim said: Abu Wael was better than me."
"4070","(4070) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Toubah al-Anbari, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Ammar said: I saw Omar praying for a genius."
"4071","(4071) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: I saw Ata’ praying on a white carpet in the mosque. It is forbidden, and there is no one between it and tawaaf."
"4072","(4072) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in praying over the grave."
"4073","(4073) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi’ ibn al-Mundhir, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Sa’id, he said: I saw my father. Saeed bin Jubayr praying on a rug and prostrating on it."
"4074","(4074) Bishr bin Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: When Ibn Umar prayed over something, he prostrated. Aliyah"
"4075","(4075) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Toubah Al-Anbari, he said: I heard Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani He says: Qais bin Abbad Al-Qaisi prayed for his animal, Labad."
"4076","(4076) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said, I once saw Al-Hamdani praying for Forever"
"4077","(4077) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to pray on a blanket with his feet and knees on it, and his hands and face on the ground, or on his burrow."
"4078","(4078) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: He told us who saw Abraham and Al-Hasan praying on a carpet in it. Pictures."
"4079","(4079) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: The prayer upon the soul is modern."
"4080","(4080) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The prayer upon the soul is modern."
"4081","(4081) Ziyad bin Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Salih Al-Dahhan; Jabir bin Zayd disliked praying over every animal, and he preferred praying over every animal. Earth plant."
"4082","(4082) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Abdullah did not He prays, and only prostrates on the ground."
"4083","(4083) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’qil bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdul Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no problem. By blessing the earth and what it produces."
"4084","(4084) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour and Husayn. Sufyan said: Or one of them, on the authority of Abu Hazim. Al-Ashja'i, on the authority of his lady, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I heard Abu Bakr forbidding prayers over baraids."
"4085","(4085) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He hated to prostrate on anything other than the ground."
"4086","(4086) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went out May God bless him and grant him peace. One night and his companions were waiting for him for the last evening prayer, and he said: The people slept and slept, and you You are waiting for the prayer, but you are not waiting for the prayer for it. Were it not for the weakness of the weak and the arrogance of the elder, I would have delayed this. Prayer until midnight. (Abu Ya’li 1935; Ibn Hibban 1529)"
"4087","(4087) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, who said: Whoever entered The mosque was in its state, and he would not stop spending time in it as long as he was in it, until he left it, or spoke."
"4088","(4088) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It used to be said, if a man prayed and then sat in his place of prayer, then he In a prayer, and the angels pray over him unless it occurs during it, and if he sits in the mosque, he is in a prayer unless he It happens, and as long as it does not cause harm in it."
"4089","(4089) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Aban, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: There is no man who prayed a prayer. And he waits for another, except that the angels say: Your servant is so-and-so, O God, have mercy on him so that he may pray for her."
"4090","(4090) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, who said: If a man is sitting In the mosque he waits for prayer, so he is in seclusion."
"4091","(4091) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Ayyash Al-Hadrami, he said: Yahya bin Maimun, the judge of Egypt, told us: Sahil bin Saad told me: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever waits for prayer is in prayer as long as he does not perform it. (Ahmad 5/331, Abu Ali 7546)"
"4092","(4092) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God was prepared. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, an army until midnight, or it was there, then he came out to us and said: The people prayed and slept, and you You are waiting for the prayer, but you are still praying as long as you have waited for it. (Ahmad 3/367, Abu Ali 1936)"
"4093","(4093) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: If one of you enters the mosque while he is praying, the prayer does not detain him, and the angels pray upon him. Is there one of you who, as long as he is in the place where he prayed, says: O God, forgive him, O God, have mercy on him, O God, repent to him? Unless it causes harm, unless it happens to it. (Bukhari 477, Abu Dawud 560)"
"4094","(4094) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman, who said: A man from the Prophet’s companions narrated to us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If one of you prays, he completes his prayer, then sits in His prayer is the remembrance of God, and he is in prayer, and the angels pray upon him, saying: O God, have mercy on him and forgive him. And if he entered his prayer place and waited, it would be like that. (Ibn Saad 174)"
"4095","(4095) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was detained on the authority of His companions were in the evening prayer, until a third of the night remained, and he came to them while some of them were standing and some of them were sitting. And some of them were lying down, and he said: You have continued to pray since you have been waiting for it, the one standing, the one sitting, and the one lying down."
"4096","(4096) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: None of you will cease to be in Pray as long as prayer imprisons you."
"4097","(4097) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, delayed One night he continued the prayer until half-way through the night, and the people were praying and reclining, so he left and his band remained and he prayed. With them, when he greeted them, he turned to face them and said: The people have prayed and fallen asleep, and you have not ceased to pray since you have waited. Prayer, he said: It is as if I am looking at the sparkle of his ring on his hand. (Bukhari 847. Muslim 222)"
"4098","(4098) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sadaqa ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: They used to resemble the prayer Al-Hajir by praying in the middle of the night."
"4099","(4099) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, who said: Pray the prayer of the Ja’ir, We used to like it."
"4100","(4100) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: Pray the evening prayer when The fay is given when the call is made at noon, and whoever prays it, it is as if he had prayed at night."
"4101","(4101) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, on the authority of their father, who said: Alqama and I got a newspaper, and we took it to Abdullah, where we sat at the door while the sun had set, or was almost set. So he woke up and sent the maid, and said: Look who is at the door. So she returned to him and said: Alqamiya and the lions, so they said: He called me to them, so we entered, and he said: It is as if you have been sitting at the door for a long time? They said: Yes. He said: What prevented you from asking our permission? They said: We feared that you might be asleep. He said: I did not like you to think of me like this. This is an hour that we used to liken to. With the night prayer."
"4102","(4102) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The prayer of the people of faith after noon."
"4103","(4103) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Aoun; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on tanned fur."
"4104","(4104) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq; He used to tan the skin of his sacrifice, so he would take it as a place of prayer and pray over it."
"4105","(4105) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ismail ibn Raji, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; He used to tan the skin of his sacrifice, so he would take it as a place of prayer and pray over it."
"4106","(4106) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad and his companions; They hated to pray over furs."
"4107","(4107) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Khabab, who said: I entered upon Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad in Al-Madain and he was He prays in his home on the skin of a sheep, the wool visible above his feet."
"4108","(4108) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, who said: Suwayd bin Ghafali used to say “Allahu Akbar” when the muezzin said, “The prayer has risen.” Prayer"
"4109","(4109) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” when the muezzin said, “The prayer has begun,” meaning “in the beginning.”"
"4110","(4110) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If I were to hear the muezzin making his voice after... Abraham says “Allahu Akbar” for the prayer."
"4111","(4111) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he wishes, he should say “Allahu Akbar” when he says, “The prayer has begun,” and if He wanted to wait until he finished."
"4112","(4112) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhall, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to say “Allahu Akbar” when the muezzin said, “The prayer has begun.” The second"
"4113","(4113) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan?? He hated for the imam to stand until the muezzin said, “The prayer has begun,” and he hated for the imam to say “Allahu Akbar” until the muezzin had finished speaking. His residence"
"4114","(4114) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was when the muezzin said, “Hayy `Ali.” He performed the prayer, so when he said, “The prayer has begun,” he said “Allahu Akbar.”"
"4115","(4115) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, he said: He would remain silent until the muezzin finished, then he would say “Allahu Akbar.” And Abraham used to say, “Allahu Akbar” when the prayer began."
"4116","(4116) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatadah, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When the prayer is performed, do not get up until you see it. (Bukhari 6371, Muslim 156)"
"4117","(4117) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, on the authority of Zayd ibn Nashit, on the authority of Abu Khaled al-Walbi, who said: He revolted against me. The prayer had been performed and they were standing and waiting for him. He said: Why do I see you standing still?"
"4118","(4118) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They hated for a man to stand up if the muezzin said, The prayer had begun, but they did not have the imam, and they hated to wait for the imam to stand up, and it was said: He is the Samud."
"4119","(4119) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, who said: I said to Ibrahim: The people are waiting. Is the imam standing or sitting? He said: No, but sitting."
"4120","(4120) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the people waiting for the imam to stand, he said: That is the eternal prayer."
"4121","(4121) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, who said: I heard him say: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz, with his pinky fingers, says when the muezzin says, “The prayer has begun”: “Arise, the prayer has begun.”"
"4122","(4122) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated for the imam to stand until the muezzin said, “The prayer has begun.”"
"4123","(4123) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazid saw Hussein bin Ali in the Zamzam Basin. The prayer was performed, and a quarrel arose between the imam and some people, and the herald called out: The prayer has been performed, so they started saying to him: Sit, and he says: The prayer has begun."
"4124","(4124) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir bin Yazid bin Murah, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali. He said: If a man enters and the muezzin is performing the prayer, he says: Let him stand as he does if he wants, for that is kind to the old man. Amer said: There is no harm in it."
"4125","(4125) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I was informed that Abraham went to the mosque and the muezzin took the call. Iqama, so he put his foot between the shade and the courtyard until he finished the Iqama."
"4126","(4126) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, who said: Suwayd said: If I were able, I would I give the call to prayer and I lead them. He said: I mentioned that to Musab bin Saad, and he said: This is not from the Sunnah. Muezzin and imam."
"4127","(4127) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Asbagh, who said: Ibn Umar used to give us the call to prayer and lead us in prayer. Traveling"
"4128","(4128) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Dirār ibn Murā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abi Dhayl al-‘Anazi, who said: Omar said: Had it not been a Sunnah, I would have given permission."
"4129","(4129) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi al-Sha’tha’i, who said: It was said to Al-Aswad ibn Hilal: Come forward, and he said: Do you have lands?"
"4130","(4130) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Qais Al-Hadrami narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Eizar bin Jarul; A group of people complained to Ali about their imam, and Ali said to him: You are an idiot. You are leading a people while they are reluctant."
"4131","(4131) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Abu Ubadī al-Naji narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever leads a group of people while they are in distress, his prayer will not be valid."
"4132","(4132) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: Three prayers that do not exceed one prayer. One of them is his head; An imam of a people who hate him, a woman who disobeys her husband, and a slave who is more loyal than his master."
"4133","(4133) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith. Ibn Al-Mustaliq, he said: It was said: He is the most severely tormented person. A woman disobeys her husband, and the imam of a people, and they hate him (Tirmidhi 359)"
"4134","(4134) Hushaym told us, he said: Hisham bin Hassan told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are three whose prayers will not be accepted; A man who leads a group of people while they are his hosts, and a slave if he stays until he returns to his master, and a woman if she spends the night as a migrant. For her husband, disobedient to him. (Ibn Majah 971)"
"4135","(4135) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: I heard al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara mentioning; Salman was led by people to lead them in prayer, but he refused until they pushed him away. When he led them in prayer, he said: Are all of you satisfied? They said: Yes. He said: Praise be to God. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: There are three whose prayers will not be accepted; The woman leaves her house with righteousness, her permission, and the slave who returns, and the man who leads the people and they are his servants."
"4136","(4136) Ali bin Hassan bin Shaqiq narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There are three whose prayers should not go beyond their heads until they return; An absent slave, a woman who spent the night while her husband was displeased with her, and the imam of a people who hated her. (Tirmidhi 360 and Tabarani 8098)"
"4137","(4137) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: He went out on a journey and came forward. He led them in prayer, then said: Either you should seek an imam other than me, or you should pray alone."
"4138","(4138) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of the sheikhs of Muharib, who said: Hudhayfah said: You will seek an imam other than yourself, or You will pray alone."
"4139","(4139) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Hasten to the call to prayer, but do not hasten to lead the imam."
"4140","(4140) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan bin Uqba Abi Kibran, that he said: We were with Al-Dahhak, and he said: If he was among you Whoever comes forward should call the call to prayer and pray. He said: They refused, so we prayed alone."
"4141","(4141) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Asim, who said: Abu Ubaidah led a group of people who passed by, and when he left, he said: Satan continued to attack me until I saw that the superiority was mine over those behind me, and I would never lead a prayer again."
"4142","(4142) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Hudhayf used to lag behind the Imamate. He said: So the prayer was performed one day. He said: Then Abdullah lagged behind. He said: Then Hudhafi came forward. When he finished his prayer, he said to them: You will seek, or speak to someone else, an imam other than me, or you will pray alone. He said: Mujahid said: Abu Muammar said, on the authority of Hudhayfah that he said: Or you will pray alone. He said: So Ibrahim said: Or he said: You will pray alone."
"4143","(4143) Hushaym told us, he said: The common people told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Al-Dhail told us, he said: He was a sheikh from Those old men led his people in prayer, then he left that. He said: Then some of his brothers met him and said to him: Why did you leave the imam of your people? He said: I hate for a passerby to pass by and see me praying and say: This man did not come forward except that he is the best of them, and God does not. I will never lead them."
"4144","(4144) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: I was with Ibn Sirin at his funeral, so when we left The time for prayer came, he said: When it was performed, it was said to Ibn Sirin: Come forward, he said: So he said: Let some of you come forward, and only those who come forward may come forward. He read the Qur’an, he said, then he said to me: Go forward, so I went forward and led them in prayer, and when I finished I said to myself: What have I done? I approached him about something that Ibn Sirin hated for himself, so I said to him: May God have mercy on you, you ordered me to do something. Do you hate yourself? He said: I hate for a passerby to pass by and say: This is Ibn Sirin, who leads the people in prayer."
"4145","(4145) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ikrimah bin Ammar al-Yamami informed us, on the authority of Damm bin Jus al-Hafani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hanzala bin Al-Rahib said: Omar bin Al-Khattab led us in prayer, but he forgot to recite in the first rak’ah, so when he stood In the second rak'ah, he recited the Opening of the Book twice and two surahs, and when he finished the prayer, he prostrated twice."
"4146","(4146) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; He forgot to recite the first two, so he recited the last two."
"4147","(4147) Asbat narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he forgets to recite in the first two verses, he recites in The other two."
"4148","(4148) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, and Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I used to stand behind the lions until the muezzin came down."
"4149","(4149) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Behind the Imam will stand what is between him. And between the two rak'ahs, if anyone comes, otherwise he stands on his right."
"4150","(4150) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: You saw me standing behind Stay on top of it until someone enters, or a muezzin comes down."
"4151","(4151) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Qais Ibn Abaya, he said: Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abaya narrated to me. Unknown, on the authority of his father, he said, I have never seen a man among the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who had the most severe misdeed in Islam. From him, he said: My father heard me reciting: {In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} He said: O my son, beware of narrating hadiths, for they may I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman, but I did not hear any of them say that. If you recite, say: {Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds}"
"4152","(4152) Hushaym told us, saying: Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas, that Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman were They begin the recitation with {Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds}"
"4153","(4153) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Saeed narrated to us, he said: His leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman used to begin the Qur’an with {Praise be to God} Lord of the worlds}"
"4154","(4154) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Husayn al-Mu’allim informed us, on the authority of Badil, on the authority of Abu al-Jawza’i, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to begin the prayer with the takbir, and the recitation with {Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds}."
"4155","(4155) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zar, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to begin the recitation with {Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds}."
"4156","(4156) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; He used to begin the recitation with {Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds}."
"4157","(4157) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He was hiding {In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful}"
"4158","(4158) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to begin the Qur’an with {Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds}."
"4159","(4159) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn and Mughiry told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The imam is hidden in the name of God. The Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, and seek refuge, and Amen, and our Lord, praise be to You."
"4160","(4160) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Marzban, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to hide {In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful} and seeking refuge, and our Lord, praise be to You."
"4161","(4161) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: The imam recited out loud with {In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} Heresy"
"4162","(4162) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, and Ibn al-Zubayr; They did not talk to each other."
"4163","(4163) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid; Abu Bakr used to begin the recitation with {Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds}."
"4164","(4164) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim, who said, I heard Abu Wa’il opening the Qur’an with {Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds}"
"4165","(4165) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, Hammad, and Abu Ishaq about jirr? They said: Recite: (In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful) to yourself."
"4166","(4166) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: Speaking out loud (In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful) is the recitation of the Bedouins."
"4167","(4167) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, who said: I prayed behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Abu Bakr, Omar, and Othman did not speak out loud (In the name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful). (Bukhari 743. Muslim 299)"
"4168","(4168) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, Omar, and Uthman used to open the prayer with {Praise be to God} Lord of the worlds}"
"4169","(4169) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thawair, on the authority of his father; Ali did not pronounce out loud (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful)."
"4170","(4170) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: It is not uttered out loud (In the Name of God, Most Gracious). The Most Merciful)"
"4171","(4171) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Aswad, he said: I prayed Omar missed seventy prayers, but he did not pronounce them out loud (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful)."
"4172","(4172) Shazan narrated to us, he said: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Wael; Ali and Ammar did not pronounce (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful) out loud."
"4173","(4173) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, he said: Malik bin Ziyad informed us, he said: Omar bin Salih led us in prayer. Abdul Aziz, so he opened the prayer with {Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds}"
"4174","(4174) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He used to recite out loud (In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)."
"4175","(4175) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Waqa’i, who said: I heard Sa’id bin Jubayr pronouncing out loud (In the name of God, Most Gracious). The Most Merciful)"
"4176","(4176) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; Indeed, they used to recite out loud (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful)."
"4177","(4177) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr reciting: (In the name of God, the Most Gracious. The Most Merciful), then he recited: (Praise be to God, Lord of the Worlds), then he recited: (In the Name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)."
"4178","(4178) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubaid Allah ibn Umar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he opened During the prayer, he recites: (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful). Then when he finishes praising Him, he recites: (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful)."
"4179","(4179) Saul bin Yusuf and Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr; Ibn al-Zubayr used to pronounce out loud (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful) and say: Nothing prevents them from it except pride."
"4180","(4180) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of His father; Omar said out loud (In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)."
"4181","(4181) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to say: If a man recites once in his prayer (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful), that is sufficient for him."
"4182","(4182) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: When he sought refuge, he passed and recited (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful) It is sufficient for the remainder of his prayer."
"4183","(4183) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He used to recite: (In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful) in every rak’ah."
"4184","(4184) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, Hammad, and Abu Ishaq, and they said: Recite in every rak’ah. With (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful)"
"4185","(4185) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, Hammad, and Abu Ishaq; Concerning a man who recites two surahs in the rak’ah. Whenever he recites a surah, he begins with (In the Name of God, Most Gracious, Most Merciful)."
"4186","(4186) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha; He used to read from the Qur’an, so whenever he finished a surah, he would recite: (In the name of God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful)."
"4187","(4187) Ismail Ibn Aliyya narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir Ibn Shanazir, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: If A man turned to the people while they were sitting at the end of the prayer, then he entered into the double, and if he turned to them and the imam greeted, And they did not separate, so it entered into the double.\nAta’ said: It used to be said: If he left your house intending to overtake them, or did not overtake them, then he entered. In the weakness."
"4188","(4188) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Aamir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever realizes tash-hud has He completed the prayer."
"4189","(4189) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salamah, who said: Whoever leaves his house Before the imam said the salaam, he had overtaken you."
"4190","(4190) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibn Suhayb, who said: When Zirr and Abu Wa’il saw us in the row, We were children. They took us out."
"4191","(4191) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ukaym; If he saw a boy in the class, he would take him out."
"4192","(4192) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Aban Al-Attar, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim; If Omar bin Al-Khattab saw a boy in the class, he would take him out."
"4193","(4193) Sharik bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hani’ Al-Muradi, on the authority of a man from his people; Hudhayfah used to separate the boys in class, or he said: during prayer."
"4194","(4194) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, or Hilal, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, he said: Ali said: The muezzin has authority over the call to prayer, and the imam has authority over By residence"
"4195","(4195) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, he said: They were waiting for the lions, and he Imam"
"4196","(4196) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, he said: They were waiting for the Imam until... The muezzin comes down."
"4197","(4197) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Ma`qil ibn Abi Bakr; Omar bin Al-Khattab waited after the prayer was performed."
"4198","(4198) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, who said: The prayer was established and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. A survivor greeted a man next to the mosque, and he did not get up to pray until the people fell asleep. (Bukhari 642, Muslim 284)"
"4199","(4199) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Omar would have resisted the man after it was established. Prayer"
"4200","(4200) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: The prayer was established and the rows were lined up, so he retreated. A man came to Omar and he spoke to him, so they prolonged their standing until they were thrown to the ground while the people were in rows."
"4201","(4201) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalababi, and Ibn Sirin; When they recited the prostration, they would greet each other."
"4202","(4202) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman; He used to say “Peace be upon you” when he recited the prostration."
"4203","(4203) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: I saw Abu Al-Ahwas reciting the prostration and then he gave the salutation on his right. Peace be upon you"
"4204","(4204) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Ibrahim, Abu Salih, and Yahya bin Wathhab did not submit to Islam. prostration"
"4205","(4205) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; When he recited the prostration, he did not say the salutation during it."
"4206","(4206) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Al-Hasan used to recite for us the prostration of the Qur’an, but he did not say the salaam."
"4207","(4207) Abbad told us, on the authority of Waqaqi bin Iyas Al-Asadi, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He used to recite the prostration, but he would raise his head and not say the salutation."
"4208","(4208) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Abu Al-Ashhab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that they said: When he recites The man who prostrates, let him say “Allahu Akbar” when he raises his head, and when he prostrates."
"4209","(4209) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, and Ibn Sirin, that they said: If a man recites When he prostrated in something other than a prayer, he said: God is Greatest."
"4210","(4210) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, who said: Whenever my father recited the prostration, he would say: God is Great, then he prostrated."
"4211","(4211) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman; He used to recite the prostration while walking, so he would say “Allahu Akbar” and gesture wherever his face was, and he would say “Allahu Akbar” when he raised his face."
"4212","(4212) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: When you recite the prostration, say “Allahu Akbar.”"
"4213","(4213) Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: We used to read about Abu Abd al-Rahman while we were walking. When he passed the prostration, he said “Allahu Akbar” and nodded and said “salaam.” He claimed that Ibn Masoud used to do That"
"4214","(4214) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; The companions of Abdullah used to recite the prostration while they were walking, and they would nod."
"4215","(4215) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad; He used to recite it while walking, and he would nod."
"4216","(4216) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya; Indeed, he was a Messenger."
"4217","(4217) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: I asked Kurdous about the prostration. The man recited it while he was He walks? He said: My day."
"4218","(4218) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad, he said: Ammar bin Al-Qaqa’ narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Zur’i bin Amr bin Jarir; He mentioned gesturing, and I mentioned to him that Abraham recited it while he was walking, so he gestured."
"4219","(4219) Abdi told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taimiy, who said: I used to show it to my father and he would show it to me. On the road, he passed by the prostration and prostrated, so I said to him: Should you prostrate on the road? He said: Yes."
"4220","(4220) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Razi, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Anas, who said: I said to Abu Al-Aliyah: I am taking a narrow path, and I hear the reciter reciting the prostration, so I prostrate on the road? He said: Yes, prostrate on the road."
"4221","(4221) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Muhammad; Ibn Masoud used to recite while walking, and the prostration would come and he would step aside and prostrate."
"4222","(4222) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, who said: So You recited the prostration while you were walking, so place your forehead on the first wall you encounter."
"4223","(4223) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man reciting a prostration, then reciting it again. They said: The first prostration is sufficient for him."
"4224","(4224) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you recite the prostration, it is sufficient for you to prostrate with it once."
"4225","(4225) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman; He used to recite the prostration and prostrate, then he would repeat it repeatedly in that sitting, without prostrating."
"4226","(4226) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, he said: They hated shortening the prostration."
"4227","(4227) Hushaym, Ali bin Musir, and Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, who said: They were They disliked shortening the prostration, and they disliked, when they came to prostrate, to go beyond it until they prostrated."
"4228","(4228) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, he said: Three of what he narrated People: Shortening the prostration and raising the hands in supplication. Hashim said: And I forgot the third."
"4229","(4229) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Qurayr, who said: I asked Ibn Sirin about shortening the prostration? He thought about it and frowned, and said: I don’t know what this is."
"4230","(4230) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: It is from what the people have narrated."
"4231","(4231) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated that it be shortened. prostration"
"4232","(4232) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was disliked for the prostration of the Qur’an to be shortened."
"4233","(4233) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, he said: It is among the The most recent people."
"4234","(4234) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Bura, who said: I asked Ibn Umar, while I was coming from Medina, about The man recites the prostration while on an animal? He said: My day."
"4235","(4235) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man reciting the prostration while on his mount, he said: He nods with his head to the place where his face was."
"4236","(4236) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I was walking with Abu Ubaidah. Between Kufa and Al-Hira, he recited the prostration, so I went down to prostrate, and he said: It will reward you if you nod your head. He said: And he nodded his head."
"4237","(4237) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thawair, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali; He used to recite the prostration while on his camel, and he would nod."
"4238","(4238) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, who said: He used to recite the prostration on his camel, then he would gesture."
"4239","(4239) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thawair, who said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr reciting the prostration while he was on His mount, so he gestures."
"4240","(4240) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man reciting the prostration while on his riding animal, he said: He is gesticulating."
"4241","(4241) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Shebak, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: When he recites the prostration while on his animal, he nods with his head."
"4242","(4242) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mas’ar narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us; That Abraham asked Alqamah: Should he get off his mount to prostrate? So he ordered him not to come down."
"4243","(4243) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The prostration is only On the one who sits with her."
"4244","(4244) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Omar said: Prostration is only in the mosque, And when mentioned."
"4245","(4245) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Awwam, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Prostration is only for the one who sits with her."
"4246","(4246) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Prostration is only upon the one who sits with him and listens to him."
"4247","(4247) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Uthman, he said: Prostration is upon the one who sits with her."
"4248","(4248) Hushaym told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; A storyteller was sitting close to his seat and reciting the prostration, but Sa`id did not prostrate when he heard it. He said: So it was said To him: What prevents you from prostrating? He said: I did not sit with him."
"4249","(4249) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, Nafi’, and Sa’id bin Jubayr. They said: Whoever heard When prostrating, he must prostrate."
"4250","(4250) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, who said: Salman al-Farisi entered the mosque. And there are people reciting the Qur’an, so they recited the prostration and prostrated, and his companion said to him: O Abu Abdullah, had not these people come to us? The people, so he said: Why did we go out in the morning?"
"4251","(4251) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu al-Ala’, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said: I asked him about the man who was tamari. In prostration, did he hear it or not? He said: And he heard it, so what? Then Mutarrif said: I asked Imran bin Husayn about a man who does not know whether he should hear the prostration or not? He said: He heard it, so what?"
"4252","(4252) Waki’ and Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Prostration is only upon those who He heard it"
"4253","(4253) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaab, and Al-Hasan, who said: Omar said: It is not in Al-Mufassal. Prostration."
"4254","(4254) Hushaym told us, Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aryan Al-Mujasha’i, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is not in Al-Mufassal. Prostration."
"4255","(4255) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to say: There is no The detailed prostration."
"4256","(4256) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: There is no prostration in the mufassal."
"4257","(4257) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he used to say: There is no prostration in Arabic, meaning The detailed"
"4258","(4258) Abdi told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, Ikrimah, and al-Hasan, they said: There is no The detailed prostration."
"4259","(4259) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ayman bin Nabul, who said: I heard Tawus saying: There is no prostration in the joint."
"4260","(4260) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar, On the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, he said: I recited to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the star, but he did not prostrate. (Bukhari 1073. Abu Dawud 1399)"
"4261","(4261) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Yasar, he said: I asked Ubayy ibn Ka'b: What is the detailed prostration? He said: No."
"4262","(4262) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no prostration in the joint."
"4263","(4263) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Qais, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata` ibn Yasar, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Kaab, he said: There is no prostration in the joint."
"4264","(4264) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Ata bin Mina, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: We prostrated with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, {when the heavens split open}, and {recite in the name of your Lord who created}"
"4265","(4265) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated in: “When the heavens split open” (Ibn Majah 1059. Ahmad 2/247)"
"4266","(4266) Hushaym told us, he said: Ali bin Zayd bin Jad’an told us, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: I prayed behind my father. He saw the last night in Medina, and he said: So he recited “When the heavens were torn apart” therein, and he prostrated therein, and I said to him: “You shall prostrate.” In it? He said: I saw my friend Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrating in it, so I will not give up that. (Tahawi 357)"
"4267","(4267) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He prostrated The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the star, and no one remained but prostrated with him, except an old man who took a handful of dirt and raised it up. To his forehead, he said: I saw him killed as an infidel. (Bukhari 3972, Abu Dawud 1401)"
"4268","(4268) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjouf, he said: Abu Rafi’ al-Sayegh narrated to us, he said: Omar led us in prayer. He prayed the last evening prayer, so he recited in one of the first two rak’ahs: {When the heavens split open} so he prostrated, and we prostrated with him."
"4269","(4269) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: I saw Omar and Abdullah prostrating in {when The heavens were split open}, or one of them."
"4270","(4270) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Ibn Al-Asbaaniy, on the authority of Abu Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud; He used to prostrate in {when the heavens split open}."
"4271","(4271) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated in the star, and so did the Muslims."
"4272","(4272) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud; He used to prostrate in Al-A`raf, and the Children of Israel, and Al-Najm, and: {Recite in the name of your Lord who created}"
"4273","(4273) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah; Indeed, he prostrated in the star and {Read in the name of your Lord who created}"
"4274","(4274) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: The moments of prostration; (Al-Am Tanzil) and (Ham Tanzil) and (An-Najm) and {Read in the name of your Lord who created}"
"4275","(4275) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited “By the Star,” and the Muslims, the polytheists, the jinn, and mankind prostrated therein."
"4276","(4276) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Qasamah bin Zuhayr, who said: He used to prostrate in the star, and {When the heavens split open}"
"4277","(4277) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Suleiman bin Habib, who said: I prostrated with Omar. Ibn Abdul Aziz in {When the heavens split open}"
"4278","(4278) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I saw Abraham prostrating in {when the heavens split open}."
"4279","(4279) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He used to prostrate in the star, and in {Read in the name of your Lord} unless he recites them in a written prayer, for he would not prostrate or bow with them."
"4280","(4280) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad recited: {When the heavens split open} while I was sitting, so he prostrated. There it is."
"4281","(4281) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Ammar recited on the pulpit: “When the heavens split open,” then He came down to the place and prostrated therein."
"4282","(4282) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ali ibn Zayd, on the authority of Zurara ibn Awfa, on the authority of Masruq ibn Al-Ajda’; Othman recited the night prayer by the star, so he prostrated."
"4283","(4283) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Huraira said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated and the Muslims in (the star) prostrated, except for two men from Quraysh who wanted to With that good fortune (Ahmad 2/304)"
"4284","(4284) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I saw Abdullah He prostrates in {when the heavens split open}."
"4285","(4285) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid, he heard Ibn Abbas say: In (PBUH) He prostrated himself and recited: (Those are those whom Allah has guided, so follow His guidance.)"
"4286","(4286) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdah, and he told the truth, they heard Ibn Umar say: In (PBUH) he prostrated."
"4287","(4287) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: I had not prostrated in (PBUH) until al-Sa’ib narrated to me that Othman prostrated in it."
"4288","(4288) Hushaym told us, saying: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; Omar used to prostrate in (PBUH)."
"4289","(4289) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn and Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to prostrate in (PBUH) and recite these verses: {Those are those whom Allah has guided, so He followed their guidance}"
"4290","(4290) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He saluted and prostrated in (PBUH)."
"4291","(4291) Hushaym told us, he said: The Awwam told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Surah (may God bless him and grant him peace) while he was on the pulpit. When he came to prostrate, he recited it, then descended. So he prostrated."
"4292","(4292) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Positive, prostration (PBUH)"
"4293","(4293) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: It was mentioned by Ibn Abbas, and he said: {Those Those whom Allah has guided, so He followed His guidance."
"4294","(4294) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: A peacock was prostrating in (PBUH)"
"4295","(4295) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, who said: I witnessed Al-Hasan and he recited the prostration that was in (PBUH), so he prostrated."
"4296","(4296) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq; He used to prostrate in (PBUH)."
"4297","(4297) Abu Muawiyah bin Amr told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: Abu Abdul Rahman used to prostrate In (PBUH)"
"4298","(4298) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Shayba, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I saw Al-Dahhak bin A Qays prostrating in it (may God bless him and grant him peace). He said: I mentioned it to Ibn Abbas, and he said: He saw Omar bin Al-Khattab prostrating in it."
"4299","(4299) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he said: He prostrated, then recited: {Those are those whom Allah has guided, so follow His guidance.}"
"4300","(4300) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah; He did not prostrate in (PBUH) and say: Repentance is a Prophet."
"4301","(4301) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: (PBUH) was mentioned in the presence of Abdullah, and he said: Repentance of a prophet."
"4302","(4302) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Dawud informed us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, saying: It was Abdullah does not prostrate in (PBUH) and say: Repentance of a Prophet."
"4303","(4303) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’an, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: Some of the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He prostrates in (PBUH), but some of them do not prostrate, so whichever you wish, do it."
"4304","(4304) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais, who said: Abu Al-Malih did not prostrate in (PBUH)"
"4305","(4305) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard him narrating on the authority of Al-Dahhak ibn Qays; He delivered a sermon and recited: (PBUH) So he prostrated in it, and Alqamah and the companions of Abdullah were behind him, but they did not prostrate."
"4306","(4306) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha; The companions of Abdullah did not prostrate in prayer (may God bless him and grant him peace)."
"4307","(4307) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to prostrate in the last two verses of (Ham) of prostration."
"4308","(4308) Hushaym told us, saying: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il; He used to prostrate in the afterlife."
"4309","(4309) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to prostrate in the afterlife."
"4310","(4310) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to prostrate in the afterlife."
"4311","(4311) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Ibn Abbas used to prostrate with the afterlife."
"4312","(4312) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of a man from Banu Sulaym; He heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrating in (Ham) according to the first verse."
"4313","(4313) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to prostrate with the first one."
"4314","(4314) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah’s companions used to prostrate in the first manner."
"4315","(4315) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman; He used to prostrate with the first verse of (Ham)"
"4316","(4316) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I met Abraham, Abu Salih, Talha, and Yahya. And Zubaida Al-Yami; They prostrate with the first verse of (Ham) as a prostration."
"4317","(4317) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; Indeed, they were prostrating with the first verse of (Ham) of prostration."
"4318","(4318) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar; He prostrated twice during the Hajj, then he said: This surah was preferred over all the other surahs with two prostrations."
"4319","(4319) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Abdullah bin Al-As’ar; He prayed with Omar bin Al-Khattab, so he recited the Hajj and prostrated twice during it."
"4320","(4320) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Yazid bin Khumayr, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubayr bin Nufayr, On the authority of his father; Abu Al-Darda’ prostrated twice during Hajj."
"4321","(4321) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: In Surat Al-Hajj there are two prostrations."
"4322","(4322) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Abdullah Al-Ja’fi told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Salami, on the authority of Ali; He prostrated twice during Hajj."
"4323","(4323) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman; He used to prostrate twice during Hajj."
"4324","(4324) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of a man from the people of Taif, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; He prostrated twice during Hajj."
"4325","(4325) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, who said: I heard Abu Al-Aaliyah say: In Hajj there are two blessed prostrations. Two good ones"
"4326","(4326) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw people prostrating during Hajj for seventy years. You prostrated."
"4327","(4327) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, and Abi Abd al-Rahman; They used to prostrate twice during Hajj."
"4328","(4328) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Al-Aryan Al-Mujashi’i, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: During Hajj, he prostrated One"
"4329","(4329) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that he used to say: In Hajj One prostration."
"4330","(4330) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: During the Hajj, he prostrated once."
"4331","(4331) Hushi?? told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say regarding prostration: This is the first prostration of Surah Al-Hajj."
"4332","(4332) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab and al-Hasan, who said: During Hajj, one prostrates One, the first of the two.\n (4332) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: There is only one prostration in Hajj, and this is the first."
"4333","(4333) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’an, he said: I said to Jabir bin Zaid: A man prostrated twice during Hajj? He said: No one should prostrate except one."
"4334","(4334) Abdullah bin Idris and Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; Concerning a man who hears prostration while he is praying, he said: He does not prostrate."
"4335","(4335) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He does not prostrate."
"4336","(4336) Qasim bin Malik told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba; Concerning a man who hears prostration while he is praying, he said: He does not prostrate."
"4337","(4337) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Do not include in your prayer the prayer of others."
"4338","(4338) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He prostrates when he leaves."
"4339","(4339) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Harim, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about a man standing He is praying, and a man is praying close to him, so he recited the prostration. Should he prostrate when he hears it? He said: No."
"4340","(4340) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to say: If a man hears prostration while he is praying, let him prostrate."
"4341","(4341) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He prostrates."
"4342","(4342) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: When Abdullah’s companions heard the prostration, they prostrated. They were praying, or otherwise."
"4343","(4343) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Hammad about a man who was praying and heard the prostration? He said: He prostrates, and the ruling said the same thing."
"4344","(4344) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man hears the prostration while he is praying, let him prostrate. Prostrating."
"4345","(4345) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to say in a state of impurity when he heard the prostration: He should wash himself, then recite it and prostrate with it, even if he did not. He recited another one, then prostrated."
"4346","(4346) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Hammad, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, They both said: If a person in a state of ritual impurity hears the prostration, he should wash himself, then prostrate."
"4347","(4347) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to say that a menstruating woman should hear the prostration. He said: Do not prostrate. Rather, you will abandon what is greater than the prostration, the prayer. What is written?"
"4348","(4348) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr and Ibrahim about a menstruating woman listening Prostration? They said: She does not have to prostrate. Prayer is greater than that."
"4349","(4349) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to him: What do you think if a menstruating woman passes by a people? They were reading the Qur’an and prostrated. Will you prostrate with them? He said: No, I was prevented from doing something better than that, prayer."
"4350","(4350) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha (h) and on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a menstruating woman hears If you prostrate, then do not prostrate. Rather, you will neglect something more obligatory than that."
"4351","(4351) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; A woman in a state of impurity and a menstruating woman heard the prostration, but he said: They do not prostrate."
"4352","(4352) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Aban al-Attar, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Uthman, he said: She nods her head."
"4353","(4353) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: She nods her head and says: Oh God, I prostrate to You."
"4354","(4354) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Zakaria bin Abi Zayd told us, he said: Abu Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of a man, He claimed that it was like himself, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: Abdullah bin Omar used to get off his camel and catch fire. Water, then he rides and recites the prostration and prostrates, and he did not perform ablution."
"4355","(4355) Hushaym told us, saying: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who hears the prostration while he has not performed ablution, so there is no prostration for him."
"4356","(4356) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: When he heard it while he was not pure. Let him perform ablution, then recite it and prostrate. If he does not perform it well, he should recite another verse, then prostrate."
"4357","(4357) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Concerning a man reciting the prostration without having performed ablution. He said: He prostrates where his face is."
"4358","(4358) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who hears the prostration but has not yet performed ablution. He said: If he has water, he will perform ablution and prostrate, but if he does not have water, he will perform ablution and prostrate. He performed tayammum and prostrated."
"4359","(4359) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Kurayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man reciting the prostration while he is not facing the direction, should he prostrate? He said: Yes, there is no problem with it."
"4360","(4360) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: He used to recite the prostration. And he was on the other side of the qiblah as he walked, so he nodded his head, then said his salutations."
"4361","(4361) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, who said: I heard Al-Hasan and he recited the prostration that was in (PBUH), so he prostrated to Ali. He turned it into a cylinder, then he said to the people: Go towards it."
"4362","(4362) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman; He used to recite it while sitting, so he would face the Qiblah and prostrate."
"4363","(4363) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Dawud informed us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He used to say: If a man recites the prostration after the afternoon prayer and after the dawn prayer, let him prostrate."
"4364","(4364) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that they said: Read. And prostrate at any time after the afternoon prayer and after dawn."
"4365","(4365) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked the ruling about a man who recites the prostration after the afternoon prayer? Al-Hakam said: Raja’ ibn Hiyawah came to us at the time of Bishr ibn Marwan, and he was a storyteller for the common people, and he used to recite the prostration. After the afternoon prayer, he should prostrate. Shu’abi said: And I asked Hammad, and he said: If it is at the time of prayer, then there is no problem."
"4366","(4366) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salem, Al-Qasim, Ata’, and Aamer; What about a man reciting the prostration after the afternoon prayer, and before the sun rises, then he prostrates? They said: Yes."
"4367","(4367) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If you recite the Qur’an and perform prostration after the afternoon prayer and after For lunch, prostrate."
"4368","(4368) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: What prevents them from that is only laziness."
"4369","(4369) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Maqsim; A storyteller used to recite the prostration after dawn and prostrate, but Ibn Umar forbade him, but he refused to finish it, so he counted him. And he said: They do not understand."
"4370","(4370) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit bin Amara, on the authority of Abu Tamim al-Hajjami, who said: I used to recite the prostration. After dawn, I prostrated, then Ibn Umar sent to me and dissuaded me."
"4371","(4371) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Sa’id bin Abi Al-Hassan used to read after lunch, and he would pass by With prostration, he passes it, and when the prayer begins, he reads it and prostrates."
"4372","(4372) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, who said: I saw Al-Hasan reciting the Sajdah after the afternoon prayer, and when the sun had set he recited it. Then he prostrated."
"4373","(4373) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Utba. That Abu Ayyub used to recite Hadith, so when the sun rose, he recited the prostration and prostrated."
"4374","(4374) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sulaym ibn Hayyan, on the authority of Abu Ghalib; That Abu Imamah used to dislike prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun had set, and after dawn prayer until the sun had risen, and he used to The people of Syria recite the prostration after the afternoon prayer, so when Abu Imamah saw that they were reciting a surah in which he prostrated, After the afternoon, he did not sit with them."
"4375","(4375) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He heard a storyteller reciting the prostration before the prayer came, so the storyteller and those with him prostrated, so Ibn Umar took him by the hand, and when I sacrificed, he said to me: O Nafi’, prostrate with us the prostration that the people prostrated other than this time."
"4376","(4376) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq; He used to prostrate twelve prostrations in the Qur’an, which they prostrate in. He did not mention about them: {If The heavens split."
"4377","(4377) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, who said: Ali Masruq counted twelve prostrations in the Qur’an. He did not mention what is in {When the heavens split open}."
"4378","(4378) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aryan Al-Mujashi’i, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and they mentioned prostration The Qur’an, and he said: Al-A’raf, and the thunder, and the bees, and the Children of Israel, and Maryam, and Hajj is one prostration, and the ants, and the Criterion And (Al-Mat-e-Tanzeel), and (Ham-e-Tanzeel), and (PBUH), and he said: And there is no prostration in the detail."
"4379","(4379) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud; He used to prostrate in Al-A`raf, and the Children of Israel, and the star, and {Recite in the name of your Lord who created}, and {when the heavens split}"
"4380","(4380) Hushaym told us, Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Yusuf al-Makki, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr; He said: The pillars of prostration are: (Alam Revelation), (Hamm Revelation), Al-A`raf, and the Children of Israel."
"4381","(4381) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mihran, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. On the authority of Ali, he said: The pillars of prostration of the Qur’an: “Was not the revelation of the prostration,” “Hamm the revelation” of the prostration, the star, and “Recite in the name of Your Lord who created)"
"4382","(4382) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, meaning Ibn Iyas, on the authority of Ja’far; Saeed bin Jubayr said: The pillars of prostration are: (Al-Maam Revelation), Al-Najm, and {Read in the name of your Lord who created}."
"4383","(4383) Abu Asama told us, he said: Thabit bin Amara told us, on the authority of Abu Tamimah Al-Hajjimi; Indeed, sheikhs from the Banu al-Hajjim sent a rider for them to Medina and to Mecca, to ask them about prostration. The Qur’an, so he returned to them and informed them that they had agreed upon ten prostrations."
"4384","(4384) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I entered the mosque and saw two sheikhs reciting One of them was reciting the Qur’an to the one who recited the Qur’an, so I sat next to them, and behold, one of them was reciting Qays Ibn al-Sakan al-Asadi, and behold, the other was reciting. Surat Maryam, and when he reached the prostration, Qais bin Sakan said to him: Leave it, for we hate for the people of the mosque to see us. So he left it and recited what came after it. Qays said: By God, only Satan turned us away from it. He recited it, so he recited it and we prostrated."
"4385","(4385) Hushaym and Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: They used to hate it when they came upon Ali. The one who prostrates is to go beyond it until they prostrate."
"4386","(4386) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man passing by the prostration during prayer, and he said: It is not appropriate for him to pass by it and leave it."
"4387","(4387) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not appropriate for him if he passes by her. He leaves it, but prostrates with it, and if he wishes, he kneels with it."
"4388","(4388) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, he said: Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Mahrez, he said: While Al-Ash’ari was giving the Friday sermon when he recited the last prostration of Surah Al-Hajj, he said: So he came down from the pulpit. He prostrated, then returned to his seat."
"4389","(4389) Hushaym told us, he said: The Awwam told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited Surah Sajdah (PBUH) on the pulpit, and when he came to Sajdah, he recited it, then descended. So he prostrated."
"4390","(4390) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq Al-Kufi informed us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Bashir; He recited his prostration (may God bless him and grant him peace) while he was on the pulpit, so he came down and prostrated, then returned to his seat."
"4391","(4391) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Ammar recited on the pulpit: (When the heavens split open), then He came down to the place and prostrated therein."
"4392","(4392) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Omar recited it while he was on the pulpit, then he came down and prostrated."
"4393","(4393) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Shurayh, who said: Wahib al-Maafiri narrated to me, on the authority of Aws bin Bishr, he said: I saw Uqba bin Amir reciting the prostration on the pulpit, so he came down and prostrated."
"4394","(4394) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders; In the mirror, the prostration is recited and there are men with it, or a man, he said: They prostrate before it, but do not trust it."
"4395","(4395) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I asked Abraham about a woman reciting the prostration? He said: He is your imam."
"4396","(4396) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam; That a boy recited the prostration in the presence of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the boy waited for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to He prostrated, but when he did not prostrate, he said: O Messenger of God, is there no prostration in this surah? He said: Yes, but you were our leader in it, so if you had prostrated, we would have prostrated. (Bayhaqi 324)"
"4397","(4397) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Sulaym Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Sulaym bin Hanzali, he said: I read to Abdullah bin Masoud was a Surah for the Children of Israel. When I reached the point of prostration, Abdullah said: Recite it, for you are our imam in it."
"4398","(4398) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; Alqamiya, Al-Aswad, Masruq, and Amr bin Sharhabeel; They used to say: If the prostration is the end of the surah, it is sufficient for you to kneel with it."
"4399","(4399) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If at the end of the surah he prostrated, It is sufficient for you to kneel with it."
"4400","(4400) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He used to recite in the last evening’s prayers: “The revelation of the prostration” and he would bow with the prostration."
"4401","(4401) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, who said: I heard al-Sha`bi, and he was asked about the man who recites With prostration, which is at the end of the surah? He said: If he prostrated with it, he would stand up and recite after it, and if he wanted to bow with it, he would kneel with it."
"4402","(4402) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, saying: Utbah bin Qays narrated to me, on the authority of Mujahid; He used to recite the prostration among the Children of Israel, and what came after it, then he would bow."
"4403","(4403) Ubaidullah narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthām, he said: If the prostration is the last of the surah, then if you wish, bow down, and if you wish, then prostrate, for the bowing is with the prostration."
"4404","(4404) Ibn Numayr and Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Ash-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zaid, he said: We asked Abdullah about the Surah at the end of which there is a prostration, should he bow, or should he prostrate? He said: If there is nothing between you and the prostration except bowing, then it is near."
"4405","(4405) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, on the authority of Aisha; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say regarding the prostration of the Qur’an: He prostrated his face to the One who created it and fashioned it, and split it apart. His hearing and sight, with His power and strength. (Tirmidhi 580, Ahmed 30)"
"4406","(4406) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He used to say in his prostration: O God, to You my black prostrated, and in You my heart believed, O God, grant me knowledge that will benefit me, And a deed that raises me high."
"4407","(4407) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Al Ali, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He repeatedly said about prostrating the Qur’an at night in prostration: “His face prostrated before Him who created it, and His hearing was hardened.” And his sight, with his power and strength. (Abu Dawud 1409. Ahmed 217)"
"4408","(4408) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroubah, on the authority of his leaders; Indeed, when he recited the prostration, he used to say, “Glory be to our Lord, if the promise of our Lord is to be fulfilled,” Glory be to God and praise be to Him, Glory be to God. And praise be to Him, three times."
"4409","(4409) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I entered the mosque and saw two sheikhs reciting One of them was reciting the Qur’an to the one who recited the Qur’an, so I sat next to them, and behold, one of them was reciting Qays Ibn Sakan Al-Asadi, and the other was reciting to him. Surah Maryam, and when he reached the prostration, a Qais said to him: Leave it, for we hate it for the people of the mosque to see us, so they left it. He recited what came after it, then Qays said: By God, none has turned us away from it except Satan. He recited it, so he recited it and we prostrated, so when we raised Our heads. Qays said to him: Do you know what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when he prostrated? He said: Yes. He used to say: His face prostrated before Him who created it, and He weakened His hearing and sight. He said: You have spoken the truth, and I was informed that David was upon him. Peace be upon him used to say: He prostrated his face, lying in the dust, to my Creator and his right, then he said: Glory be to God! How similar are the words of the prophets to one another?"
"4410","(4410) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah recited the prostration and prostrated, Ibrahim said: Someone who heard him say about his prostration told me: “I will meet you and please you, and all goodness is in your hands.”"
"4411","(4411) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adi; Indeed, Abraham responded while prostrating."
"4412","(4412) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I said to Abraham: I recited your prostration, so I prostrated with it, so I added to it Did he prostrate again forgetting? He said: Prostrate with the prostration of forgetfulness."
"4413","(4413) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who recited the prostration while he was in an obligatory prayer, so he prostrated two prostrations. He said: He prostrates two prostrations when he has finished."
"4414","(4414) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I said to Saeed bin Jubayr: I read Prostration while I am prostrating, should I prostrate? He said: No, and why do you recite while prostrating?"
"4415","(4415) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Hatim Ibn Abi Saghira, who said: I said to Abdullah Ibn Abi Malika: I recited the prostration while I was circumambulating the Kaaba. What do you think? He said: I order you to prostrate. I said: If the people leave me while they are going around, and they say: He is crazy, can I prostrate while they are walking around? Do they go around? He said: By God, if you say so, Ibn al-Zubayr recited the prostration and did not prostrate, so Al-Harith bin Abi Rabi’i stood up and recited it. Then he came and sat down and said: O Commander of the Faithful, what prevented you from prostrating before you recited the prostration? He said: To what thing should I prostrate? If I was in prayer, I would prostrate, but if I was not in prayer, then I would not prostrate. He said: And I asked Ata about that? He said: Face the house and nod your head."
"4416","(4416) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man reciting the prostration while circumambulating the Kaaba. He said: He gestures, or he said: He prostrates."
"4417","(4417) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recited during prayer. It is written: He prostrated, then he prostrated."
"4418","(4418) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: He informed me on the authority of Abu Majliz; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited during the noon prayer. He prostrated and prostrated, so they saw that he recited: (Did not revelation) prostration"
"4419","(4419) Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; Likewise, he said: Al-Taymimi did not hear it from Abu Majliz."
"4420","(4420) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Daghfal, on the authority of Abu Hakimah; That Ibn Omar led his companions in prayer at the back, so he prostrated in it."
"4421","(4421) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, he said: Tell me who saw Ibn al-Zubayr in a wall of The wall of Mecca, he said: So he prayed the afternoon prayer, or the afternoon prayer, he said: So he prostrated, and a man said to him: You prayed five rak’ahs, so he said: I did. I recited a surah in which he prostrated."
"4422","(4422) Waki’ and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin; Ibn Masoud recited at the back of the verse: (Did not the revelation of) the prostration, and at the end with a surah from the two recited verses?"
"4423","(4423) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: Do not recite the prostration in any of written except in the Fajr prayer, and Abraham preferred to recite a surah in it on the day of Friday prayer. He prostrated."
"4424","(4424) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He did not prostrate in an obligatory prayer, and he said: I hate to add anything in an obligatory prayer."
"4425","(4425) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, who said: A man came to Omar. He said: So-and-so led the dawn prayer with us, and he recited a surah in which he prostrated. Then Omar said to him: Did he do so? He said: Yes, so Omar prayed the next day, so he recited the an-Nahl and the Children of Israel, so they all prostrated in them."
"4426","(4426) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Masruq bin Al-Ajda’, He said: I prayed the last evening prayer with Othman, so he recited by the star and prostrated in it, then he got up and recited: By the figs and the olives."
"4427","(4427) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ali bin Suwayd bin Manjuf told us, he said: Abu Rafi’ told us, he said: Omar led us in prayer. The last evening prayer, so he recited in one of the two rak’ahs: {When the heavens are torn apart} so he prostrated, and we prostrated with him."
"4428","(4428) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, who said: I said to Abu Al-Aaliyah: I prayed in the mosque of the tribe of so-and-so, so he recited. Their imam was prostrating, but he did not prostrate. He said: Why did you not prostrate?"
"4429","(4429) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim; He heard Abd al-Rahman al-Araj saying: Abu Hurairah used to prostrate in {When the heavens split open}, so when it was recited and he was behind The Imam did not prostrate, so he said: Then Abu Hurairah nodded his head."
"4430","(4430) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Amr, the client of al-Muttalib; He told them, saying: I was sitting with Ibn Omar on the day of Friday prayer at Aisha’s room, and Tariq was addressing the people. On the pulpit, he recited “Al-Najm.” When he finished, Ibn Umar fell prostrating, and we prostrated with him, and the others did not move."
"4431","(4431) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who forgot to prostrate from the beginning of his prayer, and did not mention it until he was in the last rak’ah of his prayer, and he said: He prostrates. There are three prostrations in it. If he does not mention them until he has finished his prayer other than the fact that he has not yet said the salutation, he says: He prostrates. He prostrated once as long as he did not speak. If he spoke, he resumed the prayer."
"4432","(4432) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: If a man forgets to prostrate during prayer, Let him prostrate to her whenever he mentions her in his prayer."
"4433","(4433) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man who has doubts about his prostration while he is sitting and does not know whether he prostrated it or not. Mujahid said: If you wish, prostrate to it. You have completed your prayer, so prostrate two prostrations while you are sitting, and if you wish, do not prostrate it, and prostrate two prostrations while you are sitting in Your last prayer"
"4434","(4434) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he hears the prostration while he is bowing, or prostrating, that is sufficient. His bowing and prostration are part of prostration with it."
"4435","(4435) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he increased or decreased. When he greeted the people and faced him, they said: O Messenger of God, it happened. Is prayer something? He said: What is that? They said: You prayed such-and-such, so he bent his leg and prostrated twice, then he saluted and turned to face the people, and said: If anything had happened during the prayer, I would have informed you of it, but I am a human being and I forget just as you forget, so if I forget, remember me. So if one of you errs in his prayer, let him search for what is right and complete it, and if he says the salutation, he should prostrate twice. (Bukhari 401, Abu Dawud 1012)"
"4436","(4436) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata bin Saar, on the authority of Abi Saeed Al-Khudri said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If one of you doubts about his prayer, let him remove the doubt and explain it. With certainty, when he is completely certain, he bows one rak'ah and prostrates two prostrations. If his prayer is complete, then the rak'ah is The two prostrations are voluntary, and if they are incomplete, the rak’ah is the completion of his prayer, and the two prostrations are a compulsion of Satan. (Abu Dawud 1016. Ahmad 3/84)"
"4437","(4437) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abdullah, on the authority of his father, who said: I prayed with Omar for four days. Before noon in his house, and he said: If you make an illusion, be in an increase, and do not be in a decrease."
"4438","(4438) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Ali said: If he doubts the increase, And if it is short, let him pray one rak’ah, for God will not punish Ali for extra prayer, so if it is complete then it is for him, and if It was an increase that was his."
"4439","(4439) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you are in doubt and do not know, you have completed, or If you do not complete it, then complete what you are in doubt about, for God does not punish Ali for more."
"4440","(4440) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: If any of you doubts his prayer, let him investigate as much as he thinks best, and proceed accordingly. If his most doubtful thought is that he prayed three times, then let him bow. He kneels, and prostrates two prostrations, and if he thinks it is four, then he prostrates two prostrations."
"4441","(4441) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He investigates. And he prostrates twice."
"4442","(4442) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say: He looks for what he sees as lacking and completes it."
"4443","(4443) Abdi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Salem, he said: If he is in doubt and does not know whether to pray three times or four, Let him cast aside doubt and prostrate twice. I mentioned that to Al-Qasim, and he said: And I say that, and I say that. I say"
"4444","(4444) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Malik bin Anas told me, on the authority of Afif bin Amr Al-Samimi, on the authority of Ata bin Left, he said: I asked Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas and Ka'b about the one who doubts his prayer, does he pray three or four? So they both said: Let him stand and pray one rak’ah, then prostrate twice, if he prays while sitting."
"4445","(4445) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He should search and prostrate twice."
"4446","(4446) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Salem, he said: He builds on what he is certain of, it was said to him: And he prostrates. Did you prostrate? He said: Yes."
"4447","(4447) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you doubts about his prayer and does not know whether to add more or less, if so... If he doubts about one or two, let him make them one until the illusion increases, then he prostrates. You prostrated two times while he was sitting before he said the salutation, then he said the salutation. Muhammad said: Hussein bin Abdullah said to me: Did Makhul transmit the hadith to you? Muhammad said: I did not ask him about that. He said: He mentioned it on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Omar and Ibn Abbas approached one another. In it, Abdul Rahman bin Awf came and said: I heard this hadith from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Tirmidhi) 398. Ahmed 1/190)"
"4448","(4448) Kathir bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Furat, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Abi Ubaidah. ; Whenever they were in their prayer, they did not know whether they prayed three times or four, they prostrated two prostrations before they May peace be upon you"
"4449","(4449) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the afternoon prayer with us. He said the salaam with three rak’ahs, then he entered, and a man called him rose up to him. : The hellebore, and he said: O Messenger of God, so he mentioned to him what he had done, so he went out angrily, dragging his cloak until he came to the people. He said: Is this true? They said: Yes, so he prayed that rak’ah, then he gave the salutation, then he prostrated two prostrations, then he gave the salutation. (Muslim 1010, Abu Dawud 1010)"
"4450","(4450) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas and Al-Hasan, who said: He will end up with another and his mother. Then he prostrates two prostrations."
"4451","(4451) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muharib ibn Dathar, who said: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Count as much as you can, and do not You promise"
"4452","(4452) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb; Anas bin Malik sat in the third rak’ah, so they glorified it, so he got up and completed four of them, and when he said the salutation, he prostrated two prostrations, then He turned to the people with his face and said: If you are delusional, do thus."
"4453","(4453) Muhammad bin Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he does not know whether to increase or decrease, then let him prostrate twice while sitting."
"4454","(4454) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: As for me, if I do not know how many I prayed and I will repeat it."
"4455","(4455) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He who does not know whether he prayed three times, or four times. He said: He repeats it until he memorizes it."
"4456","(4456) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (H), and on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: When he prayed and left, he did not He knows how many times he has prayed, whether Shaf'a or Witr, so let him count it."
"4457","(4457) Abdi told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (H) and on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; In the same way"
"4458","(4458) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubair about doubt in prayer? He said: As for me, if it is in what was written, then I will repeat it."
"4459","(4459) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: I threw stones, but I did not know how many I threw. So I asked Ibn Umar, but he did not answer me. Then Ibn al-Hanafi passed by and I asked him, and he said: O Abu Abdullah, it will be celebrated. There is nothing. It is more important to us than prayer. If one of us forgets, he repeats it. He said: So I mentioned what he said to Ibn Umar, and he said: They are the People of the House. Understandable"
"4460","(4460) Ibn Numayr and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He celebrates the feast, so I mentioned him. To Abi Al-Duhay, and he said: Shurayh used to say: “He will celebrate his day.”"
"4461","(4461) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If you prayed and do not know how many times you prayed, then repeat it again. If you are confused, You have to do it again, so do not repeat it."
"4462","(4462) Ibn Numayr and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He celebrates the feast."
"4463","(4463) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He celebrates the feast of his wife."
"4464","(4464) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Furat, on the authority of Abdul Karim, Sa`id ibn Jubayr, and Maimun; When they were tempted to pray, they would repeat it."
"4465","(4465) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: In Volunteering is an oversight."
"4466","(4466) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to have illusions about volunteering."
"4467","(4467) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqeel narrated to me; He heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say: You prostrated forgetfulness in the voluntary prayers, just as you prostrated forgetfulness in the obligatory prayers."
"4468","(4468) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Muhammad about some illusion regarding voluntary prayers? He said: I do not know where his place is, so I said: Should I prostrate twice after him? He said: Do you liken it to what is written? As for me, if I had not done it, I would not have done it."
"4469","(4469) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders; He had no illusions about volunteering."
"4470","(4470) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Damra bin Saeed, on the authority of Anas; He prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salutation."
"4471","(4471) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama; He prostrated them after the salutation."
"4472","(4472) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father; That Ali said: You prostrated the forgetfulness after the salutation and before the speech."
"4473","(4473) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated to them after he had saluted and spoken. (Bukhari 1229. Muslim 97)"
"4474","(4474) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went and prayed one rak’ah, then he gave the salutation, then he prostrated two prostrations, then he gave the salutation."
"4475","(4475) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya; Abdullah prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after greeting him, and it was mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did so. (Bukhari 401. Tirmidhi 392)"
"4476","(4476) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Saad and Ammar prostrated after the salutation."
"4477","(4477) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith; Abu Hurairah and Al-Sa’ib Al-Qari used to say: The two prostrations are before speaking and after the salutation."
"4478","(4478) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Anas; They both prostrated, like the prostration of forgetfulness, after the salutation, then they got up and did not salute each other."
"4479","(4479) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla; He walked and said the salutations, then he prostrated two prostrations, then he gave the salutations."
"4480","(4480) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar, on the authority of his father; He made a mistake during the prayer in Syria, so he prostrated two prostrations after the salutation."
"4481","(4481) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Uqba, on the authority of Ibrahim; He prostrated to them after he had saluted."
"4482","(4482) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Ibn Buhayna; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed a prayer that we think was the afternoon prayer, so when it was the third day, he got up before he sat down. So, before he gave the salutation, he prostrated two prostrations. (Bukhari 829, Abu Dawud 1027)"
"4483","(4483) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, and Al-Zuhri, who said: Two prostrations before he said the salutation."
"4484","(4484) Abu Al-Ahwas and Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalab; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saluted the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"4485","(4485) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah; He greeted them both."
"4486","(4486) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: May peace be upon them both."
"4487","(4487) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Sa’d, and Ammar; They prayed three times, then said salutation, and it was said to them: So they fulfilled what remained for them, then they said “Allahu Akbar”, then they prostrated, then “ Peace be upon you."
"4488","(4488) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla; He prostrated to them and then greeted them."
"4489","(4489) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He greeted them both."
"4490","(4490) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Malik Ibn Iyas, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Surrender of forgetfulness. And the funeral is one."
"4491","(4491) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In your two prostrations of forgetfulness, there is peace in them."
"4492","(4492) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He narrates What is it?"
"4493","(4493) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Whatever you witness."
"4494","(4494) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and he witnessed them, then he gave the salutation."
"4495","(4495) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin was asked about the two prostrations of illusion, What are you witnessing? He said: I would love to see him testify in them."
"4496","(4496) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: There is no forgetfulness in your prostration as tashhuhud. And no greetings."
"4497","(4497) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is neither tashahud nor tasleem in them."
"4498","(4498) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Anas; They prostrated to each other, then they got up and did not salute each other."
"4499","(4499) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The imam recites the tashahud in the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"4500","(4500) His youth told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, about Al-Hikam and Hammad; They both said: He recites the tashahhud in forgetfulness, then says salaam."
"4501","(4501) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Prophet prostrated and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. The two prostrations of forgetfulness after he said the salaam and takbeer, so he prostrated and said takbeer while he was sitting, then he raised himself and said takbeer, then he prostrated. He said “Allahu Akbar”, then he raised it and said “Allahu Akbar”."
"4502","(4502) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Sa’d, and Ammar; They prayed three times, and it was said to them: So they fulfilled what was left for them, then they saluted, then they said “Allahu Akbar,” then they prostrated, then They said “Allahu Akbar”, then they raised themselves, then they said “Allahu Akbar” and prostrated, then they said “Allahu Akbar” and raised them up."
"4503","(4503) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abi Al-Aizar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He prostrated them both in arrogance."
"4504","(4504) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no mistake in your prostration."
"4505","(4505) Uqba bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: There is no mistake in your prostration."
"4506","(4506) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Mughiryah, Ibn Abi Layla, and Al-Batti, about a man who erred in Did you perform the prostration of forgetfulness? They said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"4507","(4507) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no mistake in your prostration."
"4508","(4508) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after speaking. (Muslim 402. Tirmidhi 393)"
"4509","(4509) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad; What about a man who forgot the two prostrations of forgetfulness until he left the mosque? He said: He does not celebrate, and Ibn Shubarmah said: He does not celebrate the prayer."
"4510","(4510) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He encountered that and repeated the prayer."
"4511","(4511) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Waddah, who said: I asked his leader, and he said: Your prostration of forgetfulness is repeated."
"4512","(4512) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: If he turns his face away from the direction of the Qiblah, he will not be raised. He did not perform the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"4513","(4513) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Nabit, who said: I said to Al-Dahhak: Should I fall down, and why should I prostrate? He said: Here, then prostrate."
"4514","(4514) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He is not upon him until he comes out. Or he speaks."
"4515","(4515) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Ali bin Mudrik, who said: Alqamiya led in prayer with us, so he prayed. We prayed five times, and when he greeted, they said to him: You prayed five times, so he turned to a man from the people and said: Is that the case, one-eyed man? He said: Yes, so he prostrated twice."
"4516","(4516) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Jabir, On the authority of Al-Sha’bi, they said: For every forgetfulness there are two prostrations."
"4517","(4517) Al-Mu’alla bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Al-Haytham bin Hamid informed us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid, on the authority of Zuhair al-Hamsi, on the authority of Thawban, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: For every mistake there are two prostrations."
"4518","(4518) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla led us in prayer, and when he sat He moved to stand, prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"4519","(4519) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, who said: Anas believed us while on a journey, and he prayed two rak’ahs of afternoon prayer with us. Then, when he sat down the second time, he forgot to say the salutation, so he went to get up, so we glorified him. When he sat, he saluted and prostrated with the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"4520","(4520) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Suhayb; A man sat in the third rak’ah and they recited the Subhanahu, then he got up and completed four of them. When he said the salutation, he prostrated two prostrations, then he turned to the people. So he said: If you are concerned, do thus."
"4521","(4521) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far and Ata, who said: The oversight is only in Increase and decrease."
"4522","(4522) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid al-Dalani, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, and ; Indeed, they used to raise their heads from prostration until their buttocks were raised, and they would sit and not prostrate. You prostrated. The forgetfulness"
"4523","(4523) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: He prayed and stood up in the two rak’ahs. He did not continue to stand up, so the people glorified Him by Him, so he sat down and did not prostrate. Therefore you prostrated as forgetfulness."
"4524","(4524) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; Concerning the one who stands in the two rak’ahs, he said: If he remembers while he is facing each other, he sits."
"4525","(4525) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a man who forgets in prayer, if he stands up straight, then he must perform two prostrations, and if he remembers before standing up straight, then he does not forget. Aliyah"
"4526","(4526) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: I prayed behind Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba. So he stood up the second time, and the people praised him, but he did not sit. So when he said the salaam and turned around, he prostrated as you prostrated to me while he was sitting, then he said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, make something. (Abu Dawud 1029. Ahmad 4/253)"
"4527","(4527) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of a statement, on the authority of Qays, who said: Saad bin Malik led his companions in prayer, so he stood up. The second rak’ah, and the people recited the tasbih with it, but he did not sit down and recited the tasbih and pointed to them, saying, “Stand up.” So he prayed and prostrated twice."
"4528","(4528) Muhammad bin Fudayl and Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Al-Araj; Ibn Buhayna told him that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up two days of noon time and forgot to sit. Even when he had finished his prayer, unless he said the salutation, he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness and saluted. (Ibn Majah 1207)"
"4529","(4529) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubair; He stood up in two rak'ahs and the people recited the tasbih, until when he realized that he had lost his mind, he continued with his prayer."
"4530","(4530) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Al-Numan bin Bashir prayed and stood up for the two rak’ahs, so they glorified him and he went on. When he finished, he prostrated with the two prostrations of forgetfulness and eloquence. Sitting"
"4531","(4531) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Al-Sha’bi: I prayed two rak’ahs, and when I wanted to sit I got up. He said: If it were me, I would have gone."
"4532","(4532) Shababi told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid; It was narrated by Abd al-Rahman ibn Shammas that Uqba ibn Aamir stood up during a prayer and was sitting on him, so the people said: Glory be to God, so he knew Those they want. So when he prayed, he prostrated two prostrations while sitting, and said: I have heard what you say, and this is the Sunnah."
"4533","(4533) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who prays two rak’ahs of the obligatory prayer, then stands. He said: If he remained standing, he continued his prayer, and lo and behold, he completed His prayer: He prostrated two prostrations while sitting after he had said the salutation."
"4534","(4534) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who prayed two rak’ahs of the obligatory prayer and forgot to recite the Tashahid until he got up, he said: When he stood upright, he continued. His prayer, and he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"4535","(4535) Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, he said: I prayed behind Al-Mughirah ibn My people, so he stood up for the two rak'ahs and did not sit, so when he finished, he prostrated two prostrations."
"4536","(4536) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Imran bin Husayn led us in prayer in the mosque. He stood up for two rak'ahs, or sat for three, and Hisham most likely thought that he had sat for two rak'ahs, so when he completed the prayer, he prostrated. You prostrated forgetfulness."
"4537","(4537) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Al-Dahhak bin Qays led the people in prayer at the back, but he did not He sits in the first two rak'ahs, and when he said the salutation, he prostrated two prostrations while sitting."
"4538","(4538) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ibn al-Zubayr prayed and gave the salutation in two rak’ahs, then he stood up to the Hijr. So he received it, and the people praised it. Then he returned and completed two prostrations. He said: I mentioned that to Ibn Abbas, and he said: To God is his father. He did not neglect the Sunnah of his Prophet. (Ahmad 1/351, Abu Ali 2597)"
"4539","(4539) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah; He said the salutation in two rak'ahs, so he stood up and performed two prostrations."
"4540","(4540) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; About a man who made a mistake in his prayer and said the salutation in two rak’ahs? He said: Then he mentioned: He said: He will continue his prayer and perform two prostrations."
"4541","(4541) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaani, who said: Ibn Abi Layla led us in prayer and gave the salutation. The two rak'ahs, so we glorified Him with it. So he stood up and completed the prayer, and when he finished he prostrated two prostrations. He said: So I mentioned that to Ikrimah, and he said: Well done"
"4542","(4542) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: When he says the salutation in the two rak’ahs, he completes and prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"4543","(4543) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, saying: Laith bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib; That Suwayd bin Qais told him, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Hudayj; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed one day, then gave his salaam and left, with only one rak’ah left to pray, and a man overtook him. He said: You forgot to perform the raka’ah prayer, so he returned and entered the mosque and ordered Bilal, and he established the prayer and led the people in raka’ah prayer, so I was informed So the people said: Do you know the man? So I said: No, unless I see him. Then he passed by me, and I said: This is him. They said: This is Talhah bin Ubaid Allah. (Abu Dawud 1015, Ahmed 401)"
"4544","(4544) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Anas, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu ہریرۃ The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed one day and said the salaam in two rak’ahs, then he departed, and Dhu al-Shamalayn overtook him, and he said: O Messenger of God, was the prayer shortened or did you forget? He said: The prayer was not lacking, and I did not forget. He said: Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He is the most truthful. The hands? They said: Yes, O Messenger of God, so lead the people in prayer with two rak’ahs. (Bukhari 7251, Abu Dawud 1001)"
"4545","(4545) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed two rak’ahs of noon prayer, then gave the salutation, and it was said to him: Is it shorter than the prayer? He prayed two more rak'ahs and said the salutation, then prostrated two more prostrations. (Bukhari 1227, Abu Dawud 1006)"
"4546","(4546) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the people in prayer. He prayed three rak'ahs, then he left, and some of the people said to him: Did something happen during the prayer? He said: What is that? They said: You only prayed three rak'ahs. He said: Is that so, O Dhul-Yadin? He was called Dhu al-Shamalayn. He said: Yes. He said: So he prayed one rak’ah and prostrated twice."
"4547","(4547) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the afternoon prayer and said the salaam in three rak’ahs, then he entered and a man stood up to him, and it was said: Al-Kharbaq, and he said: O Messenger of God, so he mentioned to him what he had done, so he went out angrily, dragging his cloak until he came to the people, and he said: Is this true? They said: Yes, he said: So he prayed that rak’ah and then gave the salutation, and prostrated two prostrations, then gave the salutation."
"4548","(4548) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, led the people in prayer two rak’ahs, then he performed the salutation, and a man called Dhu said to him: Al-Din, so he mentioned such as the hadith of Ibn Aoun and Hisham, and their hadith in which he said: Was the prayer shortened? He said: No, so he prayed two more rak'ahs, then he saluted, then he prostrated two more prostrations, then he saluted."
"4549","(4549) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’; Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam prayed and spoke, so he built on his prayer."
"4550","(4550) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Al-Zubayr said some of the prayer, and said to me with his hand: How much have I missed? He said: I said: I don’t know what you are saying? He said: How much did you pray? I said: Such and such. He said: So he prayed and prostrated twice."
"4551","(4551) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Makhoul; That Abu Al-Darda’ led them in prayer in a shed in the Levant while they were outside. He said: It rained rain that reached some of them, so when he prayed or greeted, He said: Was there not a jurist among the people who said: Oh, lighten it, for indeed we have received rain."
"4552","(4552) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaani, on the authority of Ikrimah; It is said that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed two rak’ahs of afternoon prayer, then he saluted and entered, and a man from his companions entered upon him. It is said To him: Dhul-Shamalayn, and he said: O Messenger of God, has the prayer been shortened? He said: What? He said: I prayed two rak'ahs, so he came out and said: What does Dhul-Yadin say? They said: O Messenger of God, yes, so he prayed two rak'ahs with them and prostrated twice."
"4553","(4553) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: If you perform two rak’ahs, pray two rak’ahs, even if you speak."
"4554","(4554) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr; He once prayed two rak'ahs of sunset, then he greeted and spoke to his leader, and his leader said to him: You only prayed two rak'ahs, so he prayed. He bowed, then he saluted and prostrated twice, then he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did something similar to this."
"4555","(4555) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: An imam from among the imams of the Grand Mosque was delusional, but he did not prostrate as you prostrated. The forgetfulness, some of the people prostrated, and some did not prostrate, so that was mentioned to Al-Hasan, but he did not see them prostrating, and he mentioned that. According to Ibn Sirin, he chose the actions of those who prostrated."
"4556","(4556) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim (H) and on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, they said: If The imam prostrates, so there is nothing wrong with them."
"4557","(4557) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib bin Ajlan, who said: I saw Al-Qasim and Salim praying behind an imam who had erred, but he did not. He prostrated, but they did not prostrate."
"4558","(4558) Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir ibn Hazim, who said: Hammad said: If the imam makes an illusion and does not prostrate, So they do not prostrate."
"4559","(4559) Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam told us, he said: Mas’ar told me, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about him, and Al-Hakam said: They prostrated, and Hammad said: There is nothing wrong with them."
"4560","(4560) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who enters with the imam and forgets about it, he said: The imam’s prayer is sufficient for him, and there is nothing wrong with him."
"4561","(4561) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no wrongdoing upon the one who succeeds the Imam."
"4562","(4562) Khalid bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Bakkar, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: There is nothing wrong with the one who succeeds the Imam."
"4563","(4563) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He prostrated with the two prostrations of forgetfulness, and we do not know that he omitted, so we say: You did not omit anything? He says: I spoke to myself about something."
"4564","(4564) Waki’ told us, he said: Nu’aym bin Hakim told us, on the authority of Abu Maryam Al-Thaqafi, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ali led us in prayer. Maghrib, so when he finished the prayer, he prostrated two prostrations, and we did not see him do so. When he said the salutation, we said to him, he said: Indeed, he did not do so."
"4565","(4565) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about turning around during prayer? He said: Embezzlement by Satan from the servant’s prayer. (Bukhari 751, Abu Dawud 907)"
"4566","(4566) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair said: Abu Bakr did not turn around when he prayed."
"4567","(4567) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abd al-Rahman al-Dalani, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Misra, on the authority of Zaid bin Wahhab; Omar bin Al-Khattab saw a man praying two rak’ahs after sunset and before the prayer, so he turned around and hit him with a stone. He finished the prayer and said: Do not turn around, and he did not neglect the two rak’ahs."
"4568","(4568) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, who said: God never ceases to approach the servant. As long as he is in prayer, he does not speak or turn away."
"4569","(4569) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Hayyan, who said: Ja’far bin Kathir bin Al-Muttalib Al-Samimi narrated to me. He said: Abu Al-Darda’ said: O people, beware of turning around during prayer, for there is no prayer for the one who turns around, even if you are defeated by him. Voluntary, so do not neglect what is written."
"4570","(4570) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He hated turning around during prayer."
"4571","(4571) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Atiyya, who said: Aisha said: Turning around during prayer is stealthy. Satan steals it."
"4572","(4572) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah say: If you pray, then indeed your Lord He is in front of you and you are speaking to him, so do not turn around. Ata’ said: And I have heard that the Lord says: O son of Adam, to whom do you turn? I am better for you than anyone you turn to."
"4573","(4573) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The one who turns around is not a believer. Praying that God would turn his face? God is facing him and is turning away from him."
"4574","(4574) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Munqidh, who said: If a man stands up for prayer, God will accept him. In his face, then if he turns away, he turns away from it."
"4575","(4575) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: It shortens the prayer."
"4576","(4576) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim and Al-Qasim not paying attention to each other. Their prayers"
"4577","(4577) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Labid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra, on the authority of Ka’b, said: When a man stands for prayer, God will turn towards him as long as he does not turn around."
"4578","(4578) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu Ubaidah al-Naji narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he said in His illness: Sit me down, for I have a deposit that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entrusted to me. He said: Do not turn around. One of you is in his prayer, and if he must do something other than what God has made obligatory upon him. (Tirmidhi 589)"
"4579","(4579) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Khattab al-Asfari narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hikam, saying: One of the perfect prayers is that you do not know who is from whom. Your right, nor those to your left."
"4580","(4580) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Huraim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, On the authority of Imran bin Husayn: {And those who are constant in their prayers} He said: The one who does not pay attention to his prayers."
"4581","(4581) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I never saw Abu Wael turning around during his prayer."
"4582","(4582) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sa’id, on the authority of a man from Ikrimah’s companions; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to stand in prayer without bending his neck. (Abu Dawud 25. Ahmad 1/275)"
"4583","(4583) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Ikrimah; He used to do it."
"4584","(4584) Hushaym told us, he said: Some of our companions told me on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: It was The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would stay in prayer and would not pay any attention."
"4585","(4585) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He used to say: If a mistake came upon the imam and he did not realize what Yes, let him point to those behind him."
"4586","(4586) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, he said: I saw Anas bin Malik approaching... The thing is looked at in prayer."
"4587","(4587) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurayh, who said: It was said to Ibn Umar: Indeed, Ibn Al-Zubair When he stood up to pray, he did not turn around or move. He said: But we turn around and move."
"4588","(4588) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the imam forgets and does not know how many he has prayed, consider what he will do. behind him"
"4589","(4589) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Juma’, who said: I saw Ibrahim turning to the right. And north."
"4590","(4590) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, who said: I saw a foolish son doing that."
"4591","(4591) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who forgets repeatedly during his prayer, he said: Two prostrations for all of his forgetfulness are sufficient."
"4592","(4592) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When he came to the imam and he had gone before That being said, let him prostrate with the imam, then perform what he had done previously."
"4593","(4593) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; As Abraham said."
"4594","(4594) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he precedes some of the prayers and the imam has led, he said: He prostrates with The imam, then he will stand up and make the judgement."
"4595","(4595) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; Like him"
"4596","(4596) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, and Al-Hasan. Ibn Sirin said: He decides, then He prostrates, and Al-Hasan said: He prostrates with the imam, then he gets up and performs the prayer."
"4597","(4597) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, “He prostrates with the imam, and when he departs, he stands up and fulfills what he has done.” He preceded him."
"4598","(4598) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, Ibn Umar, and Ibn al-Zubayr; Concerning a man entering with the imam after he had missed part of the prayer, they said: He should do as the imam does, so when the imam finishes his prayer, he stands. So he made up his mind and prostrated twice."
"4599","(4599) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, He said: If you miss the tashahhud in the two rak'ahs, do not sit in your rak'ah to recite the tashahhud, follow the imam."
"4600","(4600) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a man who enters the prayer having already performed a rak’ah, he does as the imam does. When he says the salutation, he stands up and performs the prayer."
"4601","(4601) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abi Al-Aizar, who said: I asked Ibrahim about a man who enters with the imam. The Imam preceded him by performing a rak’ah, and the Imam had performed a rak’ah, so what should he do? He said: If you enter with the imam, do as he does."
"4602","(4602) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Abu Jabir Al-Bayadhi, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the people in prayer while he was in a state of ritual impurity, so he repeated and they repeated. (Bayhaqi 400)"
"4603","(4603) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He led them in the morning prayer, then he mentioned that he prayed without ablution, so he repeated it, but they did not repeat it."
"4604","(4604) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim; Omar led the people in prayer while he was in a state of ritual impurity, so he repeated it, and ordered them not to repeat it."
"4605","(4605) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Yazid, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ali, who said: He celebrates Eid. And they celebrate it."
"4606","(4606) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who led a people in the month of Ramadan without having performed ablution, and he led the evening prayer with them, and he prayed Ramadan and Witr? He said: He will celebrate, but no one behind him will celebrate."
"4607","(4607) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I asked him, and he said: Repeat the prayer and inform your companions. You prayed with them while you were not pure."
"4608","(4608) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He will celebrate, but no one behind him will celebrate."
"4609","(4609) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a junub person prays With the people, he completed the prayer with them. I ordered him to wash and perform the Eid, but I did not command them to perform the Eid."
"4610","(4610) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad; He said about a man who leads the people in prayer while he is in a state of ritual impurity. He said: I love that they celebrate Eid."
"4611","(4611) Qubaisa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Bukair ibn Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, he said: If he prayed with them without ablution, he would repeat it, and they did not repeat it. Sufyan said: And I would love for him to repeat it. And they celebrate."
"4612","(4612) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Whenever Ibn Umar entered a house, he saw He brought a Qur’an before the mosque, or something like it, he took it and threw it away, and if it was to the right or left, he left it."
"4613","(4613) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husayn informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated it for a man to pray while facing the mosque was a Qur’an, or something else."
"4614","(4614) Harami bin Amara bin Abi Hafsiya told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the man who is Between him and the qiblah is the Qur’an? His thoughts"
"4615","(4615) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They hated that there be There is something between them and the tribe, even the Qur’an."
"4616","(4616) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Miqsam, who said: Ibn Abbas said: Do not pray in a house in which there are statues."
"4617","(4617) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, who said: When the mosque was built during the reign of Uthman, they made On the roof of it, I would swing it, and whenever someone entering it, he would look at it. This reached Othman, so he ordered it to be removed."
"4618","(4618) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Safiyya, on the authority of his maternal uncle Musafi’, on the authority of his sister Safiyya, Umm Mansour, She said: A woman from the people of the house, from Banu Sulaym, told me. She said: I said to Uthman bin Talha: Why did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, summon you? May God bless him and grant him peace when he left the house? He said: He said: I saw the ram’s horns and forgot to order you to cover them, and they should not be in The house is something that occupies the woman praying. (Abu Dawud 2023 and Abd al-Razzaq 9083)"
"4619","(4619) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Hamid, who said: Uqba asked Al-Hasan, he said: In our mosque there is a person sitting there. Pictures, he said: Take them out."
"4620","(4620) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Uthman, he said: Lubabah narrated to me, on the authority of her mother, and she was She serves Othman bin Affan; Othman bin Affan was praying to a coffin containing statues, so he ordered it to be rubbed."
"4621","(4621) Hushaym told us, saying: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about the mosque where part of the Qur’an is written in its qiblah? He saw no harm in it."
"4622","(4622) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated it"
"4623","(4623) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Zubair Al-Hanzali, he said: I saw Omar bin Abd Al-Aziz saw his son writing on the wall, “In the name of God,” so he hit him."
"4624","(4624) Waki` narrated to us, Sa`id bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Subaih al-Hanafi, he said: I prayed next to Ibn Umar. So I put my hand on my waist, and when he prayed, he said: This is the cross during prayer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He forbade it. (Abu Dawud 899. Ahmad 2/30)"
"4625","(4625) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha; She disliked for him to put his hand on his waist during prayer, and she said: The Jews do it."
"4626","(4626) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Thawr al-Shami narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Aisha; She saw a man placing his hand on his waist, and she said: This is how the people of Hell will be in Hell."
"4627","(4627) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Saleh, the client of the twins, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He disliked it during prayer, and he said: Satan is present in that."
"4628","(4628) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked a man putting his hand on his waist during prayer."
"4629","(4629) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ishaq bin Awaymir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Placing the hands on the waist is a relief for the people of Hell."
"4630","(4630) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Imran bin Hudayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He saw a man placing his hand on his waist while praying, so he struck his hand."
"4631","(4631) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal; He only disliked shortening the prayer, because Satan descended shortening the prayer."
"4632","(4632) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: He forbade shortening the prayer. Muhammad said: That is to place his hand on his waist while he prays. (Bukhari 1220, Abu Dawud 944)"
"4633","(4633) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Hayyan ibn Umair, who said: I was with Qais ibn Abbad, and he saw A man was praying briefly, and he said: Go to that man and tell him: He should put his hand where the hand of the one praying is standing."
"4634","(4634) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha; She disliked being shortened in prayer, and said: Do not resemble the Jews."
"4635","(4635) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace; He forbade a man to pray shortened."
"4636","(4636) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Umm Salama, the Mother of the Believers, She said: And the one who left by himself did not die until he had performed most of his prayer while sitting. (Ahmad 322. Tabarani 516)"
"4637","(4637) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, who said: I asked Aisha, did the Prophet’s prayers May God bless him and grant him peace, does he pray while sitting? She said: After the tooth destroyed it. (Muslim 506. Abu Dawud 953)"
"4638","(4638) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not die. May God bless him and grant him peace, until he prayed while sitting. (Muslim 1191, Bayhaqi 490)"
"4639","(4639) Abdullah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I have never seen Ibn Umar pray sitting, except due to illness."
"4640","(4640) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of his father, he said: I would hate to God saw me praying for him sitting without illness."
"4641","(4641) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun bin Mihran, on the authority of his father; He was asked: What is the limit for a sick person to pray sitting? He said: If the world had been presented to him, he would not have risen to it."
"4642","(4642) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, who said: I saw Anas bin Malik praying in Al-Maqsourah written with Omar bin Abdul Aziz, then he will present it to us."
"4643","(4643) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus; Al-Hasan used to pray in the shrine."
"4644","(4644) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, who said: Ali bin Hussein, Ubayy and Al-Qasim used to pray in the maqsoor."
"4645","(4645) Omar bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Zaid, who said: I saw Al-Sa’ib bin Zaid praying. What is written in Al-Maqsoorah?"
"4646","(4646) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abdullah, who was trustworthy, who said: I saw Al-Hasan praying in the shrine."
"4647","(4647) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salma bin Wardan, who said: I saw a man praying at the stone."
"4648","(4648) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Aamir bin Dhu’ayb, who said: I asked Ibn Omar about praying from behind a stone? He said: They are afraid that they will kill them."
"4649","(4649) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, he said: I saw Salim, Al-Qasim, and Nafi’ praying in the Maqsoor."
"4650","(4650) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Al-Azraq bin Qais, on the authority of Al-Ahnaf bin Qais; He disliked praying in a shrine."
"4651","(4651) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Isa al-Khayyat, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not the one that is isolated from the mosque."
"4652","(4652) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Jabala bin Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz; He hated praying in it."
"4653","(4653) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jesus, on the authority of Nafi’; When the time for prayer came to him while he was in the shrine, Ibn Umar would go out to the mosque."
"4654","(4654) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Husayn informed us, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Abu Hayyan Al-Ashja’i, and he was From the companions of Abdullah, he said: Abdullah said: Do not hasten with your imams to bow or prostrate, and if one of you raises his head and the imam If someone is prostrating, let him prostrate, then let him remain as long as the Imam did before."
"4655","(4655) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, who said: Abdullah said: So he mentioned something similar to it."
"4656","(4656) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Al-Mukhlid, on the authority of his father, said: Omar said: Whoever raises his head before the imam, let him return, and let him stay until he is seen. He has realized what he missed."
"4657","(4657) Muhammad bin Harun Al-Basri narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Kandir, who said: I prayed next to Ibn Omar and raised My head was before the imam, so he took it and returned it."
"4658","(4658) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say: If he raises his head before the imam and the imam is prostrating, let him return, let him prostrate."
"4659","(4659) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to say that."
"4660","(4660) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He returns and prostrates."
"4661","(4661) Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you raise your head before the imam, return to him. To see that the Imam has risen before you."
"4662","(4662) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mukhariq, who said: I passed by Abu Dharr in Al-Rabdhi while I was performing Hajj, so I entered upon him his abode, and I saw him praying, shortening the qiyam as much as he recited (Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar), and (When he comes Nasrallah) and he bowed and prostrated a lot. When he finished his prayer, I said: O Abu Dharr, I saw you shortening your standing and bowing a lot. And prostration? He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There is no servant who prostrates to God as prostrately as He does, or bows before Him. Raka'ah, except that God removed his sin and raised him in status because of it. (Ahmad 5/147 Bazzar 3903)"
"4663","(4663) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They mentioned prostrating the Qur’an with Aisha, and she said: It is an obligation that you have performed, or a voluntary act that you have performed voluntarily. No Muslim prostrates with the prostration you have performed except that God raises him in rank because of it. And remove his sins from him."
"4664","(4664) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Uthman, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, he said: I came Damascus, then I saw a man praying. He bowed and prostrated and did not stop. So I said: If I were to sit until this sheikh guided me, he said: So I sat down, and when he finished the prayer, I said to him: O Abdullah, is Shafa'a superior to you, or to Witr? He said: I am sufficient for that. I said: Who will be sufficient for you? He said: The honorable writers, I never prostrated except that God raised me in rank because of it, and removed from me a sin because of it. I said: Who? Are you, Abdullah? He said: Abu Dharr. I said: I have become bereaved. He left his mother and taught Abu Dharr the Sunnah. When I came to Ka’b’s house, it was said to me: He asked about you. When I met him, I mentioned to him the matter of Abu Dharr, and what he said to me. He said: So he told me the same as what he said."
"4665","(4665) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Salim ibn Abi al-Ja’d, who said: It was said to Thawban: He told us about the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: They are lying to me. I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: : There is no Muslim who prostrates to God as he prostrated except that God will raise him in rank because of it, or remove from him a sin because of it. (Muslim 225. Tirmidhi 389)"
"4666","(4666) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn; That he asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about prayer while sitting? He said: Pray standing, for that is better. Then he said: The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing, and the prayer of one who is sleeping is half of the prayer of one standing. The one sitting (Bukhari 1117. Abu Dawud 948)"
"4667","(4667) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of a sheikh nicknamed Abu Musa, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Amr said: I see it on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The prayer of one sitting is half of the prayer of one standing. (Ibn Majah 1229. Ahmad 2/192)"
"4668","(4668) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn Amr, he said: We came to Medina. Then an epidemic struck us, so much so that we prayed the tasbih sitting, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The prayer of the one sitting is half of the prayer of the one standing."
"4669","(4669) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said: The prayer of the one sitting on half of The standing prayer."
"4670","(4670) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid; Al-Sa'ib asked Aisha about the prayer while sitting? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The prayer of the one sitting is half of the prayer of the one standing. (Nasa’i 4941, Ahmad 6/227)"
"4671","(4671) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The prayer of one sitting, not cross-legged, is half of the prayer of one standing."
"4672","(4672) Hushaym told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’ Al-Kailili, he said: The prayer of the one sitting on Half of the standing prayer, unless there is an excuse."
"4673","(4673) Mu’alla bin Mansour and Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ja’far, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The prayer of one sitting is equivalent to half of the prayer of one standing. (Nasa’i) 1364. Ahmed 3/214)"
"4674","(4674) Hushaym told us, saying: Awf told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in a man praying while he was a lover, and Ibn Sirin disliked it."
"4675","(4675) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to pray in hiding."
"4676","(4676) Abdah told us, on the authority of Hisham; That his father used to pray in hiding."
"4677","(4677) Abdullah bin Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, who said: I saw Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman praying. In hiding"
"4678","(4678) Abdullah bin Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, who said: I saw Isa bin Talha praying in hiding."
"4679","(4679) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour; He saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz voluntarily praying in hiding behind the shrine."
"4680","(4680) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Sa’id bin A splint prays while hiding, so when he wants to kneel, he loosens his burqa, then gets up and bows."
"4681","(4681) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; He used to pray in hiding."
"4682","(4682) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, who said: I saw Ubaid bin Umair praying. In hiding"
"4683","(4683) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Subayh, who said: I saw Ata’ praying in hiding, meaning voluntarily."
"4684","(4684) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl ibn Sa`d al-Sa`idi, he said: I saw the men Those who tied their loincloths around their necks, like children, because of the tightness of their loins, left behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Someone said: O Women, do not raise your heads until the men do. (Bukhari 362, Abu Dawud 630)"
"4685","(4685) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: O women, when men prostrate, lower your eyes. You will not see the private parts of men due to distress. The buttons (Ahmed 387)"
"4686","(4686) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, On the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: O women, when men prostrate So lower your gaze, so that you will not see the private parts of men because of their distress. (Ahmad 3/3, Bayhaqi 16)"
"4687","(4687) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Hayyan, who said: Sulayman bin Bishr Al-Khuza’i informed me, on the authority of His uncle, Malik bin Abdullah, said: I went on a campaign with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I did not pray behind an imam whose prayer was lighter. What is written from Him. (Ahmad 5/225. Tabarani 652)"
"4688","(4688) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Suhayb, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He gave the salutation to sum up the prayer and complete it. (Bukhari 7060 and Muslim 342)"
"4689","(4689) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: It was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted intentionally, and I proposed to him intentionally. (Muslim 41. Ahmad 5/91)"
"4690","(4690) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Make the prayer permissible, for among them are the weak, the old, and the needy. (Bukhari 703 and Abu Dawud 791)"
"4691","(4691) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Abu Masoud, who said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, and he said: O Messenger of God, I am late for the lunch prayer because so-and-so takes so long in it. He said: So the Messenger of God stood up and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. I have never seen him more angry in a sermon than he was on that day. He said: O people! Indeed, among you They will disperse, so whoever of you leads the people in prayer should pass, for among them are the weak, the old, and the needy. (Bukhari 901, Ibn Majah 984)"
"4692","(4692) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah; That Muadh led his Companions in prayer and recited the Qur’an with Al-Baqarah, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Is there a fatwa? Intriguing? (Bukhari 7051. Ahmad 3/299)"
"4693","(4693) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Uthman bin Mawhib, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: The mother of your people, and whoever leads a people should be light, for among them are the weak and the great. And Dhul-Hajjah, if you pray for yourself, pray however you wish. (Muslim 1864, Ahmad 4/218)"
"4694","(4694) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Distawai, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was The lightest of people said the perfect prayer. (Bukhari 710 and Muslim 342)"
"4695","(4695) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Distawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abbas al-Jashmi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, among the Imams are those who are driven away. (Daraqutni 85)"
"4696","(4696) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Sarjis, Abi Sa’id; He heard Abu Waqid al-Laythi, the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned praying with him, and he said: He was the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he is the most gentle with people, and the most kind to himself. (Abu Ali 1444. Tabarani 3314)"
"4697","(4697) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Walid bin Al-Masir Al-Tai’i, he said: Al-Tai’i’s place informed me, On the authority of Adiy bin Hatim, he said: Whoever feels safe, let him perform the bowing and prostration, for among us are the weak, the old, the sick, and the transient. Sabil, and Dhul-Hajjah, this is how we used to pray with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Tabarani 222)"
"4698","(4698) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Thabit, who said: I prayed with Anas Al-Atmah, and he passed as long as God willed."
"4699","(4699) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Musa Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Saad, that he narrated, he said: When my father prayed In the mosque, he shortened the bowing and prostration and made it permissible, and when he prayed in his house, he prolonged the bowing and prostration and prayer, so I said to him, He said: We are imams who are to be followed."
"4700","(4700) Abdi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: I saw Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam praying a prayer. Light, so I said: You are the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the people who perform the prayers lightly. He said: We will do this quickly. Obsessiveness."
"4701","(4701) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Nasir, on the authority of Khalid al-Thawri, on the authority of Ammar, who said: Delete This prayer is before the whispering of Satan. (Abdul Razzaq 3728)"
"4702","(4702) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Hudhayfah; He taught a man, and he said: The man makes the prayer easy and completes the bowing and prostration."
"4703","(4703) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of his father, he said: He used to pray behind Abu Hurairah, he said: His prayer was similar to the prayer of Qays, who performed bowing and prostration and was permitted. He said: It was said to Abu Hurairah: This is how What was the prayer of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Yes, and I allow it. (Abu Ali 6422, Hamidi 987)"
"4704","(4704) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Abu Hurairah praying a prayer. He passed it, so I said to him: This is how the Prophet’s prayer, may God bless him and grant him peace, was? He said: Yes, and I allow it."
"4705","(4705) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, who said: When Omar was stabbed and the people were assailed, Abdul Rahman bin Awf came forward and recited the two shortest surahs in the Qur’an: {Indeed, We have given you Al-Kawthar} and {When God’s victory comes And the conquest}"
"4706","(4706) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to shorten the prayer, and perform the bowing and prostration completely."
"4707","(4707) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: They used to complete and concisely, and hasten. Obsessiveness"
"4708","(4708) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was one of the most fearful of people. Prayers and conciseness."
"4709","(4709) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Muhajir, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: I have never seen prayer in any place lighter than that between these two walls, meaning the Great Kufa Mosque."
"4710","(4710) Waki’ and Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Qays, who said: Women were like it when they passed by me. While he was praying, His servants said: Lighten it up, for it is the prayer of His servants, meaning because of its lightness."
"4711","(4711) Hushaym told us, saying: Humayd told us, on the authority of Anas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am in prayer and hear the voice of a child crying, so I pass through it. My prayer is for fear that I will make it difficult for her mother. (Tirmidhi 376, Ahmed 257)"
"4712","(4712) Ali bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, On the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I am in prayer and I want to prolong it, so I hear the boy crying. So he interrupted the prayer, as he did not like to make it difficult for his mother. (Bukhari 707, Abu Dawud 785, Ahmed 305)"
"4713","(4713) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Huwayrith al-Zarqi, on the authority of Ali ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, I hear the boy crying behind me, so I ease it. I am afraid that I will test his mother. (Abdul Razzaq 3723)"
"4714","(4714) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Al-Sawda’ Al-Nadhi, on the authority of Ibn Sabit; In the first rak'ah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited a surah of about sixty verses, and he heard a boy crying. He said: He recited three verses in the second verse. (Abu Dawud 39. Abd al-Razzaq 3724)"
"4715","(4715) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, as far as we know, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: I am in prayer and I hear the child crying, so I reduce the fear of making it difficult for his mother, or he said: that she will be tempted. His mother (Abdul Razzaq 3721)"
"4716","(4716) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of?? Saeed, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Regarding a man who joins the imam for one witr of his prayer, he said: He prays as long as he joins, and does not perform two prostrations."
"4717","(4717) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, saying: Yunus was asked about a man who missed a rak’ah of the people’s prayer, or missed it. Rakaa? He said: Al-Hasan and Muhammad were not seen prostrating on him."
"4718","(4718) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ata’; That Ibn Abbas, Ibn Al-Zubayr, Abu Saeed, and Ibn Omar; If they missed a Witr of the imam’s prayer, they would prostrate twice."
"4719","(4719) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, Ibn Umar, and Ibn al-Zubayr; They said: If he missed part of the prayer, he stood up and made up for it, and prostrated twice."
"4720","(4720) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: When a man reaches the point of prostration during the imam’s prayer, he prostrates to it again, then he prostrated two prostrations after he had finished his prayer, and when he reached the point of view, he prostrated two prostrations after he had finished He finishes his prayer."
"4721","(4721) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Like him"
"4722","(4722) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; They said: If you miss one Witr of the imam’s prayer, make up what you missed, and prostrate two prostrations while you are sitting."
"4723","(4723) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He prostrates with them, but he does not prostrate Here's another way."
"4724","(4724) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; He missed a rak'ah, so he stood up and performed voluntary prayers, then he remembered the rak'ah prayer that he had missed, and he prostrated twice."
"4725","(4725) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: He interrupts and prays the rak’ah. He said: And I think he said: And he prostrates twice."
"4726","(4726) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say about a man who performed a rak’ah with the imam, and when the imam greeted him, he thought that he had joined the beginning of the prayer with him, so he stood up. He volunteered, and Al-Hasan said: If he enters an obligatory prayer voluntarily, his prayer is invalidated."
"4727","(4727) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali; He disliked praying at full capacity."
"4728","(4728) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Qais, who said: I saw Ibrahim wearing water."
"4729","(4729) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Heel; He disliked the altar in the mosque."
"4730","(4730) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hassan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Sa`id bin Abjar, on the authority of Na`im bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Salem bin Abi Al-Ja’d, said: Do not take the altars in the mosques."
"4731","(4731) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to hate praying at the limit."
"4732","(4732) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Badr informed us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to hate praying when he was full."
"4733","(4733) Hushaym told us, he said: Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi al-Ja’d, he said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They say: One of the signs of the Hour is that altars will be established in the mosques, meaning the tawaqs."
"4734","(4734) Waki` told us, he said: Abu Israel told us, on the authority of Musa al-Jinni, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: This nation will continue, or he said: My nation will be fine as long as they do not use altars in their mosques as slaughterhouses. Christians"
"4735","(4735) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: Beware of these warriors. And Abraham did not stay there."
"4736","(4736) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: One of the signs of the Hour is that the slaughterhouses are In mosques."
"4737","(4737) Abd al-Hamid bin Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abd al-Malik, he said: I saw Abu Khalid The wallaby does not stand up during the end of the night, but it stands before the end of the end."
"4738","(4738) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, who said: I saw the mosque of Abu Dharr, but I did not see anything in it at all."
"4739","(4739) Hushaym told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: It was He prays with us in abundance."
"4740","(4740) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Nafi’ narrated to us, saying: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr praying in the tent."
"4741","(4741) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Nafa’i bin Muslim narrated to us, saying: I saw Suwayd bin Ghafli praying in the curtain."
"4742","(4742) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Huraim narrated to us, on the authority of Amr’s mother Al-Muradiyyah, she said: Al-Baraa’ bin A single person prays in a tight space."
"4743","(4743) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Waqaq bin Iyas, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr praying in the tent."
"4744","(4744) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Qatan, he said: I saw Abu Raja’ praying in the mihrab."
"4745","(4745) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: So While you are praying, do not wipe your forehead, do not blow your nose, or move the gravel."
"4746","(4746) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He is from the Jafa’i."
"4747","(4747) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Khams bin al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Buraida, who said: It used to be said, four of the jifa’i: that He wipes his forehead before leaving, or urinates standing up, or hears someone being called, then does not answer him, or blows his nose. In his prostration."
"4748","(4748) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He used to hate it for a man to wipe his forehead during prayer, and say: He is one of the dry ones."
"4749","(4749) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to wipe his forehead before he left."
"4750","(4750) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi; Concerning a man wiping his forehead before leaving, he said: This is dryness, and the arbitrator said: There is no harm in it."
"4751","(4751) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim ibn Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of al-Musayyab ibn Rafi`, he said: Abd said God: There are four types of impudence: for a man to pray uncovered, and for him to wipe his forehead before leaving, or He urinates standing up, or he hears the caller, then does not answer him."
"4752","(4752) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no problem with it, meaning to wipe. her forehead before he left."
"4753","(4753) Zaid bin Abi Al-Khandaq told us, on the authority of Malik bin Dinar, who said: I asked Salim about a man who wipes his forehead? He saw no harm in it."
"4754","(4754) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hammad, who said: There is no harm in him."
"4755","(4755) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad; Like him"
"4756","(4756) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I saw him in his garment. Thus, he wiped his forehead with it, and ordered someone to spread his hand over his forehead."
"4757","(4757) Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Similar to the hadith of Wakī`, or something similar to it."
"4758","(4758) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who sleeps behind the imam until the imam kneels and prostrates, then the sleeper wakes up. They said: He follows the imam and prays as long as he He preceded him."
"4759","(4759) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham; Concerning a man who forgets the prayers, he said: He begins with the first, then the first."
"4760","(4760) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he forgets the prayers, let him start with the first, then the first, if he fears missing out. He begins with that which he is afraid to miss."
"4761","(4761) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Rashid, who said: I slept at noon, afternoon, and sunset. And the evening meal. So I went to Ubaid bin Umair and mentioned that to him, and he said: Start with the noon and afternoon prayers, and the Maghrib prayers. And dinner."
"4762","(4762) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who forgot a prayer and remembered it at sunset, and he did not pray that prayer. He said: If he was afraid that he would pray it. This is what he had forgotten, so the time for that will pass, so he should begin with the one he fears missing."
"4763","(4763) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The first will be judged by the first."
"4764","(4764) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Hammad ibn Farwa, who said: I spilled water and forgot to I performed ablution, and I prayed the noon, afternoon, and sunset prayers. I mentioned that I prayed them without being pure, so when I woke up I asked Giving and striving, Ja`far said: And I reckon him, he said: And Sa`id bin Jubayr, so they all said to him: Perform ablution and repeat your prayer now. It starts with the first, then the first."
"4765","(4765) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of a servant of Abu Bakra, who said: Abu Bakra entered an orchard. So he walked around it and looked at it and forgot the afternoon prayer until the sun had set, so when he remembered it, he performed ablution and sat down, and when it was due, he got up and stood up. He prayed the afternoon prayer, then he prayed the sunset prayer."
"4766","(4766) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Wasil, the client of Abi Uyaynah, on the authority of a man called Saad, who said: I prayed with the people during Ramadan, then I came to my family’s house and entered it and slept for my night, my day, and my night until tomorrow. So you came to Ibn Umar and informed him? He said: So you made what? He said: I prayed the noon prayer. He said: Well done. He said: Then what? He said: I prayed the afternoon prayer. He said: Well done. He said: Then what? He said: I prayed the Maghrib prayer. He said: Well done. He said: Then what? He said: I prayed the evening prayer. He said: Well done. He said: Then what? He said: Stringed. He said: What did you do with the stringed string? He said: Then what? He said: I prayed the morning prayer. He said: Well done."
"4767","(4767) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus and Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: He who falls asleep after praying. He woke up at sunrise and said: He would pray Fajr, then he would pray Isha."
"4768","(4768) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, that he used to say: He begins with dinner. The one he slept on."
"4769","(4769) Ruh bin Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who forgets the darkness, or lies in it until dawn comes, and it is said to him: If he begins to feel the darkness, will he miss the dawn? He said: Let him start with the dark, even if he misses the morning."
"4770","(4770) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala’, he said: His leaders narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever forgets a prayer, or falls asleep during it, his atonement is that he prays it when he remembers it. (Bukhari 5971 Muslim 314)"
"4771","(4771) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Jami’ bin Shaddad, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Alqamiya, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud said: We came with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Al-Hudaybiyah, and they mentioned that they had descended Trampled on by the ground. What he means by trampled is sand. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who are we to eat? Bilal said: I am. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Then we sleep. He said: They slept until the sun rose on them. He said: Then he woke up. There were people among them so-and-so and so-and-so, and among them was Omar, so we said: Be prepared, meaning speak. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, woke up. He greeted us and said: Do as you used to do. He said: So we did. He said: Likewise for those who fell asleep or forgot. (Abu Dawud 448 Ahmad 1/386)"
"4772","(4772) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Ismail, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: We had a wedding with the Prophet. One night, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, we did not wake up until the sun hurt us, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to us: And he greeted: Let each man of you take the head of his mount, then move away from this house. Then he called for water, performed ablution, and prostrated. You prostrated two times, then the prayer was established and you prayed. (Muslim 310. Ahmad 2/429)"
"4773","(4773) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Abbas, on the authority of Aoun bin Abi Juhaifa, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on the journey in which they slept until the sun rose, then he said: You were dead, and God restored your souls to you, so whoever fell asleep after praying, or forgot to pray, let him pray it when he remembers it, and when Wake up (Abu Ya’li 895. Tabarani 268)"
"4774","(4774) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man falls asleep after praying, or forgets Let him pray when he wakes up, or remembers."
"4775","(4775) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Imran bin Husayn and Samurah bin Jundub disagreed about the one who forgets his prayer, so Imran said: He prays it when he remembers it. Samarra said: He will pray it when he mentions it and at its time from the next day."
"4776","(4776) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Sabra bin Nakhaf, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He prays when He mentioned"
"4777","(4777) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of Saad, who said: He said: He prays it when he remembers it, and he prays the same the next day."
"4778","(4778) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: Whoever sleeps or forgets a prayer, He said: He prays whenever he remembers it, at sunrise or at sunset, then he recited: (Establish the prayer for my remembrance) He said: Then I mentioned it, so pray it at whatever hour you are."
"4779","(4779) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Humaid, on the authority of Abu Malih, on the authority of Abu Dhar, and Abdul Rahman Ibn Awf; Do you forget during prayer? They said: He prays for her when he remembers her."
"4780","(4780) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Qais, on the authority of Zakaria bin Jarad, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: Did you not have anyone to protect you? Pray for my remembrance."
"4781","(4781) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi and Ibrahim, who said: {Establish the prayer in remembrance of Him} i.e. Pray it if you remember it and have forgotten it."
"4782","(4782) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah, who said: I asked Nafi’ about a man who forgot the afternoon prayer. Until the sun turned yellow? He said: He prays it, not like any of the prayers."
"4783","(4783) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam, he said: He prays it when he mentions it."
"4784","(4784) Hushaym told us, saying: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; Concerning a man who sleeps after praying the evening prayer until the sun rises, he said: He prays."
"4785","(4785) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept after the dawn prayer until the sun rose, and he said to his companions: Move away from the place. Heedlessness has afflicted you, so he prayed and then said: {Establish the prayer in remembrance of Me}"
"4786","(4786) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of some of the Banu Abu Bakra; Abu Bakra fell asleep in their dungeon and we thought he had prayed the afternoon prayer, so he woke up at sunset. He said: So he waited. Until the sun set, then he prayed."
"4787","(4787) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Malik bin Ka’b, on the authority of My father, he said: I slept until dawn until the sun rose, and we were worried about what we had, so I went to drink from the palm trees to perform ablution. He said: Then he looked at my father and said: What is the matter with you? I said: I am praying and I have performed my ablution, so he called me and made me sit next to him, and when the sun rose and became white and I came to the mosque, He hit me before I got up to pray, and said: Have you forgotten? Pray now"
"4788","(4788) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who forgets to perform a prayer until the sun turns yellow, he said: He performs it when the sun sets, and his followers said, like That"
"4789","(4789) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Qatada told us, on the authority of His father, Abu Qatada, said: We walked with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey one night. He said: We said: Messenger of God, if you were to meet us, he said: I fear that you will fall asleep and miss the prayer, so who will wake us up for the prayer? He said: Then Bilal said: I, O Messenger of God. He said: So he sat with the people and they lay down, and Bilal leaned on his camel and it defeated him. Our eyes, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up and the visor of the sun had risen, and he said: O Bilal, where is what you told us? He said: O Messenger of God, by the One who sent you with the truth, I have never been given a sleep like this. He said: Then he said: God has taken your souls. When he wanted, and he returned them to you whenever he wanted, he said: Then he ordered them to spread out for their need, and they performed ablution and the sun had risen, so he prayed. With them dawn (Bukhari 5951 Abu Dawud 441)"
"4790","(4790) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin al-Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Omar came On the day of the ditch, he started cursing the infidels of Quraysh and saying: O Messenger of God, I did not pray the afternoon prayer until the sun had almost set. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: By God, I have not prayed yet. So he went down and performed ablution, then prayed the afternoon prayer after sunset. The sun, then he prayed the Maghrib prayer after he prayed the Asr prayer. (Bukhari 945. Muslim 438)"
"4791","(4791) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, who said: We were with the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was on a journey, and indeed we passed the night until, when it was the end of the night, we encountered that event, and no He was more beautiful than her when he met a traveler. Nothing woke us up except the heat of the sun, so he made Omar say “Allahu Akbar.” When he woke up, people complained about him. Whatever happened to them, he said: There is no harm. He said: So they set out and walked for not far, then he descended and the call to prayer was made, so he led the people in prayer. (Bukhari 344, Muslim 476)"
"4792","(4792) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer (h) and on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you are in the afternoon prayer, Then you mentioned that you had not prayed the noon prayer, so he finished the noon prayer, then prayed the afternoon prayer."
"4793","(4793) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; Concerning a man who forgot the noon prayer, then he remembered it while he was in the afternoon prayer. He said: He goes away and prays the noon prayer, then he prays the afternoon prayer."
"4794","(4794) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us in his hadith: And if he mentioned it after he had prayed the afternoon prayer, then it had passed. And he prays the noon prayer."
"4795","(4795) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If he remembers while he is in prayer, he goes away and prays the noon prayer. Then he prayed the afternoon prayer."
"4796","(4796) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who mentioned a prayer while he was praying? They said: If he mentions it before reciting the tashahhud, or if he sits for the duration of the tashahhud, he will leave this one and return to that one. He mentioned it after that, took pride in that, and returned to that."
"4797","(4797) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He prays the afternoon prayer, and when he finishes, he prays the noon prayer."
"4798","(4798) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If he mentioned while he was in the afternoon prayer that he did not pray the noon prayer, So he prays the afternoon prayer, then he prays the noon prayer after that."
"4799","(4799) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say: If you remember while praying the afternoon prayer that you did not pray the noon prayer, you continue with it, then pray the noon prayer, So if you prayed the afternoon prayer and mentioned that you did not pray the noon prayer, then you prayed its parts."
"4800","(4800) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Al-Hasan, the same."
"4801","(4801) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who prayed with the people of the afternoon prayer and the afternoon prayer for him, he said: His prayer was complete, and those behind him continued the same day."
"4802","(4802) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: A single prayer is not sufficient for two people. winter"
"4803","(4803) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, who said: I went to the Jami’ Mosque and I saw that they did not They were praying the noon prayer, so I stood up and volunteered until the prayer was established. When they prayed, it was the afternoon prayer, so I stood up and prayed the noon prayer with them, then I prayed the afternoon prayer, then I went to Al-Hasan, and I mentioned that to him, so he ordered me to do the same as what you did."
"4804","(4804) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Kathir ibn Aflah, he said: We have come to The mosque and I did not pray the Maghrib prayer, so I established the prayer and prayed with them while I saw that it was the Maghrib prayer, so when the evening prayer came, So I got up and prayed the Maghrib prayer, then I prayed the Isha prayer, then I asked, and they ordered me what I had done."
"4805","(4805) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; About a man who entered with some people at noon, and he told them the afternoon prayer? He said: He begins with what God began with, praying the noon prayer, then praying the afternoon prayer."
"4806","(4806) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: I was informed about a peacock and an atta, that they said: It is sufficient for him."
"4807","(4807) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Abu Ja’far, Salim, and Al-Qasim, And a gift on the authority of a man who entered with a people during the afternoon prayer and thought that it was the afternoon prayer? They said: He will leave and pray the noon prayer, and the afternoon prayer will suffice for him. He said: I asked Amir and Muslim bin Subaih, and they said: He will leave. So he prays the noon prayer, then he prays the afternoon prayer, for God has written it down with him before the afternoon prayer, so it is not for him the noon prayer. Jabir said: On the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, like that."
"4808","(4808) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab and al-Hasan, who said: About a man who entered with A people in the afternoon prayer, and he thought they were in the noon prayer, so when they were in the afternoon prayer, he said: He will lead the two prayers. All of you"
"4809","(4809) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say about a traveler, if he forgot a prayer and remembered it while in the city: Pray the prayer of travel, and if he forgot a prayer while in If a resident remembers it while traveling, let him pray the prayer of a resident."
"4810","(4810) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, and Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like that"
"4811","(4811) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Fadl, on the authority of al-Hasan, he said: If he forgets a prayer in the city, So he remembered her while traveling, he prayed the prayer at home, and if he forgot a prayer while traveling and remembered her while at home, he prayed the prayer while traveling."
"4812","(4812) Waki’ told us, he said: I heard Sufyan say: He is praying the prayer that he had forgotten."
"4813","(4813) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abd al-Khaliq, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If he forgets a prayer in the city, he remembers it. While traveling, he prays four times, and if he forgets a prayer while traveling and remembers it while he is present, he prays a prayer while traveling."
"4814","(4814) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Al-Zubayr informed us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Abdul God, on the authority of his father; The polytheists occupied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of the ditch with four prayers, until some of the night had passed. God willing, he said: So he ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer and iqama, so he prayed the noon prayer, then he remained iqama and prayed the afternoon prayer, then he iqamamed and prayed the sunset prayer, then He stayed and prayed the evening prayer. (Tirmidhi 1791, Ahmad 1/375)"
"4815","(4815) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhib informed us, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, said: We were imprisoned on the day of the ditch for noon, afternoon, sunset and evening prayers. Until we are sufficient for that, and that is the words of God Almighty: {And God is sufficient for the believers from fighting, and God is Strong, Mighty} So the Messenger of God stood up May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he ordered Bilal to perform the prayer, then he prayed the noon prayer as he had prayed before, then he performed the iqama Asr prayer, so he prayed the afternoon prayer as he had prayed it before, then he stood for the Maghrib prayer, so he prayed the Maghrib prayer as it was before. He prayed for her before that, then he performed the evening prayer and prayed for her as he had prayed for her before that, before he came down: {Then if you fear, then on foot or mounted}"
"4816","(4816) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Omar said: Who He missed some of his recitation during the night, so he prayed what was between it and the noon prayer, as if he had prayed at night."
"4817","(4817) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abdă, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm; That a man asked Omar for permission to migrate, so he blocked him for a long time, then he gave him permission, and said: I had fallen asleep from your party. So I was the one who fulfilled it."
"4818","(4818) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abu Ubaid Allah, the client of Ibn Abbas, who said: He said: Ali: Whoever misses something from his party, and his prayer at the height of the day, it is as if he prayed at night."
"4819","(4819) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: We used to go to Aisha before the dawn prayer, so we went to her. One day, when she was praying, she said: I slept away from my party that night, so I was not going to invite him."
"4820","(4820) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, who said: Whoever misses it, his portion of the night So he made up for it before the sun had set, and he had reached you."
"4821","(4821) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: He A speech that means conquest for the Imam."
"4822","(4822) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated to open the door to the imam."
"4823","(4823) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Maymun Abi Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud; Concerning the imam’s indoctrination: It is only words delivered to him. He said: And Abraham said: I don’t care if I teach you, or I said: Oh. Big"
"4824","(4824) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays, on the authority of Salam bin Atiyya; That a man opened the prayer to a short imam while he was praying, and when he left, he said to him: Perform your prayer."
"4825","(4825) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman; He hated that the reader should be taught."
"4826","(4826) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Whoever gives Fatwa to the Imam has spoken."
"4827","(4827) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He disliked the conquest of the Imam."
"4828","(4828) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ubaidah ibn Rabi`, he said: I came to the place and saw a man, well dressed and with a fresh scent, praying. He recited the Qur’an, and a man next to him opened the door to him. I said: Who? This? They said: Othman."
"4829","(4829) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Abu Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of Ali, who said: If he gives you food The imam fed him."
"4830","(4830) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Marwan used to teach prayer and the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace in Medina."
"4831","(4831) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, that they did not see any harm. By indoctrination of the imam."
"4832","(4832) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: He was taught by an imam."
"4833","(4833) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; Ibn Mughaffal ordered a man to teach him if he learned something."
"4834","(4834) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Musawar, he said: Hilal bin Abi Hamid told me, he said: I used to open the door to Abdullah Ibn Uqaym used to pray with one another, and one day he said to me: Didn’t you pray with us? He said: So I said: No. He said: I denounced that. I hesitated yesterday but did not find anyone to open up to me?"
"4835","(4835) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in indoctrinating the imam."
"4836","(4836) Ma’an bin Issa told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, who said: I was praying next to Nafi’ bin Jubair bin Mutim, and he winked at me, so I opened to him while he was praying."
"4837","(4837) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar led us in prayer, he said: He hesitated, he said: So I opened for him. So he took it from me."
"4838","(4838) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: We used to greet the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he prayed and responded to us, before we came to the land of Abyssinia, and when we came from the land of Abyssinia I greeted him, but he did not respond to me, so he took hold of me near and after, and when he finished his prayer, he said: Indeed, God speaks of His command. Whatever he wanted, he decided that you should not speak during the prayer. (Abu Dawud 921. Ahmad 1/377)"
"4839","(4839) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me. He greeted me on a need, so I came while he was praying, so I greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. (Abu Dawud 923. Ahmad 3/379)"
"4840","(4840) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Peace be upon the one praying incapacitated."
"4841","(4841) Hafs and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakariya, who said: I said to Al-Sha’bi: Enter a people while they are praying alone. Do I greet them? He said: No."
"4842","(4842) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He responds to him in himself."
"4843","(4843) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of a man from Banu Amir, who said: I stood beside Abu Dharr was praying, so I greeted him, but he did not respond to me."
"4844","(4844) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Busr bin Saeed, he said: A man greeted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, and he pointed to him with his hand, as if he was concluding it."
"4845","(4845) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We used to greet him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in prayer before we went out to the Negus and he would respond to us. When we returned from Al-Najashi: I greeted him, but he did not respond, and said: There is a preoccupation in prayer. (Bukhari 1199, Abu Dawud 920)"
"4846","(4846) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I asked Suhayb, how was he? What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do where he used to greet him? He said: He was gesturing with his hand. (Abu Dawud 922. Tirmidhi 367)"
"4847","(4847) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, who said: I greeted Ibn Abbas while he was praying in front of me. The Kaaba, so he took it by the hand."
"4848","(4848) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I greeted Ibn Abbas while he was praying, but he did not respond to me. He extended his hand to me and shook my hand."
"4849","(4849) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Abu Ayyad, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: If he greets you while you are praying, then respond."
"4850","(4850) Hafs and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I would not greet Ali. A man was praying. Abu Muawiyah added: If he had greeted me, I would have responded to him."
"4851","(4851) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If one of you greets one of you while he is in As for the prayer, let him wave his hand."
"4852","(4852) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He was asked about a man who greets him during prayer? He said: He responds by slitting his right head."
"4853","(4853) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who greets him during prayer, he said: He returns the greeting to him when he departs, so when he goes, he follows him with the greeting."
"4854","(4854) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: When Abdullah came from Abyssinia, he came to the Prophet and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace while he was praying, so he greeted him and he nodded and pointed with his head."
"4855","(4855) Waki` bin al-Jarrah narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah; That a man greeted Ibn Abbas while he was praying, so he took his hand, shook it, and winked his hand."
"4856","(4856) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan saying: He does not return the greeting until he prays, so if he is near, return it. Even if he is far away, follow him with greetings."
"4857","(4857) Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, he said: Asim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, he said: He was asked about a man who greets him while he is praying? He said: When he performs the prayer, follow it with salutations."
"4858","(4858) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Ibn Al-Hanafi, on the authority of Ammar, who said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was praying, and I greeted him. He said: He returned my greetings. (Ahmad 4/263, Abu Ali 1634)"
"4859","(4859) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdul Rahman bin Muwaib, on the authority of his paternal uncle, on the authority of a servant of Abu Sa’id. The numb one; He was with Abu Sa`id Al-Khudri, and he was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he saw a man sitting in the middle of the mosque, crossing his fingers and talking to himself. He said: So he nodded. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went to him but he did not think so. He turned to Abu Sa’id al-Khudri and said: If one of you prays, do not He interlaces them between his fingers, for interlacing is from Satan, and one of you does not stop praying as long as he is in the mosque. Until he comes out of it. (Ahmad 3/54)"
"4860","(4860) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Yazid bin Khusaifi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When one of you is in the mosque, he should not interlace his fingers."
"4861","(4861) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Thumama Al-Qammah, he said: I found Ka'b while I was on the floor, and I had inserted some of my fingers into each other. He struck my hand severely, and said: We are forbidden to We interlace our fingers together in prayer. He said: I said to him: May God have mercy on you, do you see me in prayer? He said: Whoever performs ablution and goes to the mosque, then he is in prayer. (Abu Dawud 563. Ahmad 4/241)"
"4862","(4862) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Abi Ayyash, he said: They used to forbid Interlacing the fingers, meaning in prayer."
"4863","(4863) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Muhall, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked interlacing his fingers during prayer."
"4864","(4864) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalifa bin Ghalib, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I saw Ibn Umar intertwining between His fingers during prayer."
"4865","(4865) Hushaym told us, he said: Our companions told us, about Al-Hasan; He used to interlace his fingers in the mosque."
"4866","(4866) Affan narrated to us, he said: Wahib narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, he said: I saw Salim bin Abdullah networking. between his fingers during prayer."
"4867","(4867) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: If he wanted to say, “God hears those who praise Him,” then he said: God is Great. He said: May God forgive you."
"4868","(4868) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he wanted to say, “God hears those who praise Him.” He said: Allah is the Greatest, so let him not forget."
"4869","(4869) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, and others; Concerning a man who wanted to say: God hears those who praise Him, so he said: God is great. They said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"4870","(4870) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, Amir, and Ata’, they said: About a man who wanted to He says: God hears those who praise Him, and he says: God is great. They say: There is nothing wrong with him."
"4871","(4871) Wakī’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bā, he said: I asked the ruling about a man who forgot to say arrogance? He said: He prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"4872","(4872) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who prayed Maghrib four times, he said: He prostrates the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"4873","(4873) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He celebrates the feast."
"4874","(4874) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If he does not sit on the third day, he should repeat it."
"4875","(4875) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yasar, he heard Abu Hurairah say: When the prayer is established There is no prayer except the obligatory prayer. (Muslim 493. Abu Dawud 1260)"
"4876","(4876) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: So The prayer has been established, so there is no prayer except the obligatory prayer. (Muslim 493. Abu Dawud 1260)"
"4877","(4877) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He saw a man praying at the time of the afternoon prayer. He said: You would be pleased to be told: The son of so-and-so prayed six times. He said: So I mentioned That was for Abraham, and he said: It was disliked to pray with the Iqamah."
"4878","(4878) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Fudail ibn Amr, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate it. Prayer when the muezzin begins the Iqama."
"4879","(4879) Umar ibn Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Maimoon, who said: When the muezzin says “Allahu Akbar” with the Iqamah, do not pray. anything until you pray the obligatory prayer."
"4880","(4880) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Farwa, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin al-Munkadir, on the authority of Sa`id bin Al-Musayyab Omar saw a man praying two rak'ahs while the muezzin was performing the prayer, so he turned away from him and said: There is no prayer while the muezzin is performing the prayer, except for the prayer. The one for whom prayer is performed."
"4881","(4881) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you are in the mosque and perform the prayers Prayer, do not kneel."
"4882","(4882) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, that he said about a man who prays two rak’ahs of prayer in the mosque. The obligatory prayer alone, then the prayer is performed. He said: He should pray with them and not be taken into account."
"4883","(4883) Hushaym told us, saying: Sayyar and Al-Mughiry told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi (h), and Yunus and Mansour told us, On the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, they said: He says the salutation and then enters with the imam in his prayer."
"4884","(4884) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, he said: I think so, on the authority of Utbah ibn Qays, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Utbah, he said : He cuts them off and then enters with them."
"4885","(4885) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mas’ar, he said: I heard Hammad saying: I would love for him to speak and enter with them in Prayer"
"4886","(4886) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: If a man enters The obligatory prayer, then when the residence came to him, he broke it off, and it was a voluntary prayer for him, and he entered into the obligatory prayer."
"4887","(4887) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; Concerning a man who comes to the mosque and sees that they have prayed, so he assumes the prayer and prays two rak’ahs of the obligatory prayer, and the prayer is established. He said: He joins the imam in his prayer, and when he prays two rak’ahs with the imam, then he says the salutation, then he performs the two rak’ahs. The other two are with the imam voluntarily."
"4888","(4888) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, that he said: As Abraham said."
"4889","(4889) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: If a man was standing and praying and he heard Let the residence be cut off. Abraham said: He adds another to it and does not interrupt it."
"4890","(4890) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Fudayl ibn Amr, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He used to say: If he remains There is something of your prayer upon you, so complete it. Saeed bin Jubayr used to say: Cut it off."
"4891","(4891) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: If the prayer begins voluntarily The prayer was established and he completed it."
"4892","(4892) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, he said: I was next to Abdul Allah bin Maqil, and he was praying and reciting Surah An-Nur, so the muezzin stood up, so he bowed and prostrated, and he sat and recited the tashahhud, then he stood up with the imam So he took it from where he left."
"4893","(4893) Ibn Adam told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of a statement, he said: Qays ibn Abi Hazim used to lead us as a leader, so the muezzin established Prayer, and he prayed two rak'ahs. He said: Then he left it, then he went forward and led us in prayer."
"4894","(4894) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: If you say the “Allahu Akbar” by praying voluntarily before he says the “Allahu Akbar.” By staying, pray two rak’ahs."
"4895","(4895) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you are in the mosque and the prayer is established, then do not You kneel, unless you are on a string, in which case you may intercede."
"4896","(4896) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: I wrote to Omar from Najran: They did not find a place. Cleaner, or better than what you sold? So he wrote: Sprinkle it with water and lotus leaves and pray over it."
"4897","(4897) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi. They said: There is no harm in prayer in the sale."
"4898","(4898) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about praying in churches and selling? He did not see any harm in it."
"4899","(4899) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: There is no problem. By praying in the church and selling."
"4900","(4900) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: There is no harm in praying in the church."
"4901","(4901) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated it, and Muhammad did not see any harm in it."
"4902","(4902) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khusayf, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He disliked praying in a church if there were images in it."
"4903","(4903) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Hind, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz leading the people above A church, and people are lower than it."
"4904","(4904) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Rafi’, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz leading the people in a church. In the Levant"
"4905","(4905) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Badr, on the authority of Qais bin Talq, on the authority of his father Talq bin Ali, who said: We went out as a delegation to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and we informed him that he had sold our land to us, so he accepted it as a favor. He cleaned it, called for water, performed ablution, then rinsed his mouth. Then he made it for us to treat, and said: Go out with it with you. When you come Your country, break your pledge of allegiance, sprinkle water in its place, and take it as a mosque. (Ahmad 4/23. Ibn Hibban 1602)"
"4906","(4906) Waki’ told us, he said: Abu Fadalah told us, he said: Azhar Al-Harazi told us; That Abu Musa prayed in a church in Damascus, which is called: The Church of John."
"4907","(4907) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to hate it for a man to lean on the wall during the obligatory prayer, unless he was against it, and he did not see it in it. Volunteering is great."
"4908","(4908) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated for a man to support himself against a wall during prayer, and he hated for him to raise his legs except from a height."
"4909","(4909) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He hated to raise one of his legs on it. The last one in prayer, and it is supported against a wall except on top of it."
"4910","(4910) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: His reward will be reduced by the amount of that."
"4911","(4911) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Mujahid; Regarding a man praying and leaning against a wall, he said: He detracts from his prayer by the amount of that."
"4912","(4912) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm in him leaning on the wall."
"4913","(4913) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He disliked for a man to rely on anything during the obligatory prayer except for a reason, and he saw no harm in it in voluntary prayers."
"4914","(4914) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Mu’tim bin Al-Miqdam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: No servant leaves behind his family better than two rak’ahs that he performs with them when he intends to travel."
"4915","(4915) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: When you go out, pray Two rak'ahs"
"4916","(4916) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; If he wanted to leave, he would go into the mosque and pray."
"4917","(4917) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I saw Al-Harith bin Abi Rabi’ When he wanted to go to Bagmuirah, he prayed two rak'ahs in the chamber in the morning, and a group of them prayed with him. Al-Aswad ibn Yazid"
"4918","(4918) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Muadh bin Abdullah bin Khubayb, on the authority of Jabir, who said: When we came with The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: O Jabir, did you pray? I said: No, he said: Pray two rak'ahs."
"4919","(4919) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Kamil Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Abu Salih; When Othman returned from a journey, he would pray two rak’ahs."
"4920","(4920) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you offer a chapter Two rak'ahs"
"4921","(4921) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Muqatil ibn Bashir al-Ijli, on the authority of a man called: Musa; Ibn Abbas came from a journey and prayed two rak'ahs in his house on his head."
"4922","(4922) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, on the authority of His father; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would not set out on any journey except during the day, in the morning, so when he came, he would start with the mosque and pray. Two rak'ahs (Bukhari 3088 and Muslim 496)"
"4923","(4923) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Tamim bin Salama, on the authority of Masruq, he said: It was The Prophet, may the peace and blessings of God be upon him, was on a journey, so he attended a wedding with his companions, and none of them woke up during his wedding except the sun, so he got up and gave the muezzin the call. He stood, then prayed, and Masruq said: I do not like to have this world and what is in it due to the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. After sunrise."
"4924","(4924) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Tamim bin Salama, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like him (Ahmad 1/259, Abu Ali 2375)"
"4925","(4925) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sa`d ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Ata` ibn Yassar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, the two rak’ahs of Fajr after he had crossed the valley, then he commanded Bilal to perform the adhan and iqama, then he performed the obligatory prayer."
"4926","(4926) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: It is sufficient for a man to make up the prayers. With one iqama."
"4927","(4927) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: We walked one night with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Then we said: O Messenger of God, if you The earth, so we slept and took care of our passengers? He said: Who is guarding us? He said: I said: I, he said: Then my eyes got the better of me, so he did not wake us up until the time the sun rose, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not wake up. Peace and blessings of God be upon him, except with our words. He said: So he commanded Bilal and he called the call to prayer and established the iqaamah, so he led us in prayer. (Ahmad 1/450. Tabarani 10349)"
"4928","(4928) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He did not see any harm in the number of verses in the prayer."
"4929","(4929) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Like him"
"4930","(4930) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Yasir bin Amr; He saw no harm in the number of verses in the prayer."
"4931","(4931) Abdă and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham; That his father used to count the verses in prayer."
"4932","(4932) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: Yahya bin Wathhab used to count the verses in the prayer."
"4933","(4933) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I saw a peacock and a peacock counting the verses in prayer."
"4934","(4934) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to count the verses with his left hand in prayer."
"4935","(4935) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in counting verses in prayer."
"4936","(4936) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Yahya bin Atiq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He used to count the verses in prayer."
"4937","(4937) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, who said: I saw Abu Abd al-Rahman counting the verses in Prayer"
"4938","(4938) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: I saw Ibn Abi Malika counting the verses in the prayer. So I said to him? He said: He is the best at heart."
"4939","(4939) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Yahya ibn Atiq, who said: I saw a peacock and al-Mughirah ibn Hakim Al-Sana'ani enumerates the verses in prayer."
"4940","(4940) Abu Ayyub al-Quray’i narrated to us, saying: I saw Imran bin Hudayr counting the verses in prayer, and he mentioned that Abu He saw no harm in that."
"4941","(4941) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in counting a verse in prayer if there is fear of forgetfulness."
"4942","(4942) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin counting the verses in the afternoon."
"4943","(4943) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no harm in counting the verses in the obligatory prayer."
"4944","(4944) Yahya bin Bashir Al-Jazari told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in counting the verses in prayer."
"4945","(4945) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Omar, who said: I saw Ibn Abi Maliki counting the verses in prayer. He said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Sayfi said: He is the head of the servants."
"4946","(4946) Omar bin Ayyub al-Mawsili told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Marzuq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz asked him: How many verses are counted in prayer? He said: What do I do? He said: What do I do too?"
"4947","(4947) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, who said: I asked Suleiman bin Yassar about sleeping in... The mosque? He said: How do you ask about this, when the people of Saffah used to sleep in it and pray in it?"
"4948","(4948) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: I saw Ibn Sirin sleeping in the mosque."
"4949","(4949) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He had a mosque in which he prayed and slept in."
"4950","(4950) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: When we were young, we spent the night in The covenant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque and a narration. (Tirmidhi 321, Ahmad 2/12)"
"4951","(4951) Jarir told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man said to Ibn Abbas: I slept in the Sacred Mosque. So she had a wet dream, and he said: As for taking it for the night or a place to stay, no, but as for sleeping and resting, or waiting for something, then no. Unfortunately"
"4952","(4952) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They disliked sleeping in the mosque."
"4953","(4953) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Do you hate sleeping in the mosque? He said: Rather, I love him."
"4954","(4954) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, he said: Mujahid forbade me from sleeping in Mosques"
"4955","(4955) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ayman bin Nabul, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr saw me while I was sleeping in the stone. So he woke me up and said: Someone like you sleeps here?"
"4956","(4956) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Amr al-Shaybani, he said: I saw Ibn Masoud was in the mosque at night, and he did not leave any darkness without taking it out, except for a man praying."
"4957","(4957) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mugheerah bin Ziyad narrated to us, saying: I used to sleep in the Sacred Mosque, so I had a wet dream in it. Last night, I asked Ataa repeatedly. He said: Sleep even if you have had a wet dream ten times."
"4958","(4958) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Hakim, on the authority of Sa’id Ibn Al-Musayyab; He was asked about sleeping in the mosque? He said: Where were the people of Suffa? That means they sleep in it."
"4959","(4959) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, he said: I slept in the Sacred Mosque and had a wet dream. So, I asked Saeed bin Jubayr? He said: Go and wash, meaning, but he did not prohibit it."
"4960","(4960) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: One night at Maimunah bint Al-Harith, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and prayed during the night, so I got up on his way. So he took hold of my wolf that was mine, or by my head, and made me stand on the right side. (Bukhari 117 Ahmad 1/215)"
"4961","(4961) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Musa ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas, he said: I came The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, so he made me stand on his right. (Muslim 2691, Ahmad 3/194)"
"4962","(4962) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Shurahbil, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I prayed with the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he made me stand on his right. (Ibn Majah 973. Ahmad 3/326)"
"4963","(4963) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of his father, who said: I came to Omar while he was praying. So I stood to his left, and he placed me on his right."
"4964","(4964) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: I prayed with him and he made me stay in prayer. His right hand"
"4965","(4965) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; A man stood up and prayed on his left, so he turned him to his right."
"4966","(4966) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If a man prayed with Ibn Abbas, he would lead him in prayer. On his right hand"
"4967","(4967) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: I entered the Damascus Mosque with an alcoholic drink while he had prayed. His family, so he made me stand on his right, and I prayed with his prayer."
"4968","(4968) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He will stand on his right."
"4969","(4969) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; When a man stood up with him, he would make him stand on his right side."
"4970","(4970) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I came to Urwah while he was praying, so he made me stand on his right."
"4971","(4971) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I asked Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab about him, and he said: He is his custodian on the authority of Yessara"
"4972","(4972) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Harun bin Antarah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, he said: Alqamah asked for permission. And the lion was on Abdullah, so he gave them permission, and said: There will be princes who will distract you from the time of prayer, so pray it at its proper time. Then he stood up and prayed between him and him, and said: This is what I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, do."
"4973","(4973) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Harun bin Antar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamah and Al-Aswad. , on the authority of Abdullah; He raised him, like him."
"4974","(4974) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he said: If they were three One of them went ahead and two fell behind."
"4975","(4975) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; When a third person prayed, he would make two people behind him."
"4976","(4976) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; When the two men prayed with him, he would follow them behind him."
"4977","(4977) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If they were three, one of them should lead them."
"4978","(4978) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, who said: If the people are three apart from the Imam, they shall come first. Someone"
"4979","(4979) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, who said: A man and I prayed with Mujahid, and one of us stood up. On his right, and the other on his left, and he said: This is how he does the three."
"4980","(4980) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of his father, who said: I came to Omar while he was praying. With Al-Hajira, I stood on his left and he put me on his right, then he came to Yarfa, but we delayed, so we became two of him behind him."
"4981","(4981) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas (h) and on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan, They said: If there were three of them, one of them would lead them and two would pray behind him."
"4982","(4982) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, he said : I came to Omar while he was praying and he placed me on his right, then Yarfa’ came and we placed him behind him."
"4983","(4983) Abu Nu’aym narrated to us, he said: Nusayr bin Abi Al-Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Khawar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Misra, on the authority of Al-Nazzal bin Sabra, on the authority of Ali, who said: If there are three of them, one of them leads them."
"4984","(4984) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Musa ibn Anas, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led them and a woman from his family in prayer, so he placed the man on his right and the woman behind him."
"4985","(4985) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Thabit, who said: I prayed with Anas, so I stood on his right, and the mother of his children stood up. Behind us"
"4986","(4986) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I came to Urwa while he was praying, and a woman was behind him, so he made me stay. On his right and the woman behind him."
"4987","(4987) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If the imam is with him, one man and one woman, Let them stand frequently."
"4988","(4988) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar Al-Daniy, on the authority of a woman from his people whose name is Hujriyah, she said Our nation, Umm Salama, was standing among the women."
"4989","(4989) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Umm al-Hasan; She saw Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, leading the women, standing with them in their row."
"4990","(4990) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha; She used to lead women in prayer in obligatory prayers."
"4991","(4991) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Aisha; She used to lead women in prayer, standing with them in class."
"4992","(4992) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi said: Women lead the women in the Ramadan prayer, standing with them in their rows."
"4993","(4993) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, that he said: There is no harm for a woman to lead in prayer. Women, stand with them in class."
"4994","(4994) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of a servant of Banu Hashim, on the authority of Ali, who said: Do not pray. The woman"
"4995","(4995) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I wrote to Nafi’ to ask him: Can a woman lead women in prayer? ? He said: I do not know of a woman who leads women."
"4996","(4996) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Tell me who saw Jabir bin Zayd gesticulating in water. And clay."
"4997","(4997) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: When he was in water and mud, he gestured gesturing."
"4998","(4998) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Aamir, who said: The one who is in the water and the mud gesticulates."
"4999","(4999) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you are in water or marsh, Then he nodded."
"5000","(5000) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; Concerning a man who is overtaken by prayer in water and mud. He said: He gestures and makes prostration lower than bowing."
"5001","(5001) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prostrating in water and mud. (Bukhari 669 and Muslim 826)"
"5002","(5002) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, who said: I came with Anas bin Malik from Kufa, Even when we were high, and the sky had taken us before that, and the earth was shallow, so Anas prayed while he was on a donkey facing forward. He kissed him, gestured, and made prostration lower than bowing."
"5003","(5003) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Salem and Amer, who said: If you are in... Water and mud. You do not find a place to prostrate, so nod your head."
"5004","(5004) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ghalib bin Sulaiman, on the authority of a man from Haddan, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; He fell into water and mud and began to kneel, so when he wanted to prostrate he gestured, so I said to him? He said: O fool, do you want me to spoil my clothes?"
"5005","(5005) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Dammam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered the killing of the two lions during prayer, the snake and the scorpion. (Ibn Majah 1245. Ahmad 2/248)"
"5006","(5006) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, who said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man He prays sitting, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Why do you pray sitting? He said: I was stung by a scorpion. He said: If one of you sees a scorpion, even if he is praying, let him take off his left shoe. Let him kill her with it."
"5007","(5007) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila; That Ali killed her while he was praying."
"5008","(5008) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar; Ibn Umar saw a feather while he was praying, so he thought it was a scorpion, so he struck it with his shoe."
"5009","(5009) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Al Aliyah; He killed her while he was praying."
"5010","(5010) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in killing her while he was praying."
